            {"type": "score", "title": "Q13 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Four postulates of the Cartesian sign convention", "body": "Know first: Refraction and reflection at a single spherical surface. Taking the pole \\( P \\) as origin: (1) Rays are always incident from the left on the refracting or reflecting surface. (2) All axial distances to the right of \\( P \\) are positive and to the left of \\( P \\) are negative. (3) The acute angle a ray makes with the axis (or normal) is positive if the axis (or normal) rotates anticlockwise to coincide with the ray, and negative if clockwise. (4) All transverse distances measured upward perpendicular to the axis are positive and downward are negative.", "tex": "u < 0 \\text{ (left)}, \\; v, R > 0 \\text{ (right)}, \\; y > 0 \\text{ (upward)}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Summary of sign rules", "tex": "1.\\; \\text{Incident rays: left to right, origin at pole } P \\\\ 2.\\; x > 0 \\text{ right of } P, \\quad x < 0 \\text{ left of } P \\\\ 3.\\; \\theta > 0 \\text{ anticlockwise from axis/normal, } \\theta < 0 \\text{ clockwise} \\\\ 4.\\; y > 0 \\text{ upward from axis, } y < 0 \\text{ downward}", "body": "List the incident direction, axial distance rule, angle rotation rule, and transverse height rule. Four postulates 4 · clarity/example 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the sign convention, incident rays always travel from ____.", "options": ["left to right", "right to left", "top to bottom", "bottom to top"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Rays are conventionally incident from the left on the optical surface."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The angle between the axis and a ray is positive if the axis is rotated through an acute angle ____.", "options": ["anticlockwise to the ray", "clockwise to the ray", "by 180 degrees", "perpendicular to the ray"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Anticlockwise rotation from the reference line is taken as positive."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For a real object placed in front (to the left) of a refracting surface, the object distance \\( u \\) is ____.", "options": ["negative", "positive", "zero", "infinite"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Distances to the left of the pole P are negative."}
          ]
