            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 5 marks", "title": "Question 14", "marks": 5, "q": "For an interference pattern ,find the ratio of intensity at P to that at maximum such that path difference S2P - S1P = \\lambda / 3 ."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Phase difference calculation and cosine-squared intensity ratio", "options": [{"t": "Phase difference 2pi/3 and intensity ratio I/I_max = 1/4 found", "m": 5}, {"t": "Correct phase difference 2pi/3 but arithmetic error in ratio", "m": 3}, {"t": "Formula I = I_max cos^2(delta/2) stated only", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Convert path difference to phase difference and evaluate cos^2(delta/2)."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q14 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Intensity ratio I / I_max = 1 / 4", "body": "Know first: Interference of light waves. A path difference of \\( \\Delta = \\lambda/3 \\) corresponds to a phase difference \\( \\delta = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\lambda}\\Delta = \\frac{2\\pi}{3} \\). Using \\( I = I_{\\max}\\cos^2(\\delta/2) \\), the ratio of the intensity at \\( P \\) to the maximum intensity is \\( \\cos^2(\\pi/3) = \\frac{1}{4} = 0.25 \\).", "tex": "\\frac{I}{I_{\\max}} = \\frac{1}{4} = 0.25"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Intensity ratio from path difference", "tex": "\\Delta = S_2P - S_1P = \\frac{\\lambda}{3} \\\\ \\delta = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\lambda}\\Delta = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\lambda}\\cdot\\frac{\\lambda}{3} = \\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\text{ rad} \\\\ I = 4I_0\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\delta}{2}\\right) = I_{\\max}\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\delta}{2}\\right) \\\\ \\frac{I}{I_{\\max}} = \\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{4}", "body": "Find the phase difference delta from the path difference and substitute into the cosine-squared intensity law. Formula 1.5 · phase difference 1.5 · ratio 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Phase difference \\( \\delta \\) is related to path difference \\( \\Delta \\) by ____.", "options": ["2 pi Delta over lambda", "pi Delta over lambda", "lambda Delta over 2 pi", "Delta over lambda"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "A path difference of lambda corresponds to a phase difference of 2 pi."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For two equal-intensity coherent waves, resultant intensity \\( I \\) equals ____.", "options": ["I_max cos^2(delta/2)", "I_max sin^2(delta/2)", "I_max cos(delta)", "2 I_max"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Superposition of two equal waves gives I = 4 I0 cos^2(delta/2)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When the path difference is \\( \\lambda/3 \\), the ratio \\( I/I_{\\max} \\) is ____.", "options": ["one fourth", "one half", "three fourths", "zero"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "cos^2(pi/3) = (1/2)^2 = 1/4."}
