            {"type": "eval", "q": "Fringe width formula, unit conversion and numerical answer", "options": [{"t": "Formula beta = lambda D / d and beta = 0.05 cm (0.5 mm) with units", "m": 5}, {"t": "Correct formula and substitution with minor unit/arithmetic slip", "m": 3}, {"t": "Only formula beta = lambda D / d written", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Convert d, D, lambda to consistent units and compute beta = lambda D / d."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q15 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Fringe width beta = 0.05 cm (0.5 mm)", "body": "Know first: Interference of light waves. The fringe width in Young's double-hole experiment is \\( \\beta = \\frac{\\lambda D}{d} \\). With \\( d = 0.5\\text{ mm} = 0.05\\text{ cm} \\), \\( \\lambda = 5\\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm} \\), and \\( D = 50\\text{ cm} \\), we get \\( \\beta = 0.05\\text{ cm} = 0.5\\text{ mm} \\).", "tex": "\\beta = 0.05\\text{ cm} = 0.5\\text{ mm}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of fringe width", "tex": "d = 0.5\\text{ mm} = 0.05\\text{ cm}, \\quad \\lambda = 5 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm}, \\quad D = 50\\text{ cm} \\\\ \\beta = \\frac{\\lambda D}{d} \\\\ \\beta = \\frac{5 \\times 10^{-5} \\times 50}{0.05} = 5 \\times 10^{-2}\\text{ cm} = 0.05\\text{ cm} = 0.5\\text{ mm}", "body": "Substitute the given values in centimeters into the fringe-width formula. Formula 1.5 · substitution 1.5 · answer with units 2."},
