            {"type": "score", "title": "Q17 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Fresnel zone plate", "body": "Know first: Fresnel diffraction and zone plate. A zone plate is a specially constructed screen consisting of concentric circles whose radii are proportional to the square roots of natural numbers (\\( r_n \\propto \\sqrt{n} \\)), with alternate annular zones made opaque. By blocking either all even or all odd Fresnel half-period zones, the remaining zones interfere constructively at the focus, so the zone plate acts like a converging lens with multiple foci \\( f_m = \\frac{r_1^2}{(2m-1)\\lambda} \\).", "tex": "r_n = \\sqrt{n f \\lambda}, \\quad f_1 = \\frac{r_1^2}{\\lambda} = \\frac{r_n^2}{n\\lambda}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Zone radii and focal length", "tex": "\\frac{1}{v} + \\frac{1}{u} = \\frac{n\\lambda}{r_n^2} = \\frac{1}{f_1} \\\\ r_n = \\sqrt{n f_1 \\lambda} = r_1 \\sqrt{n} \\\\ A_{\\text{res}} = A_1 + A_3 + A_5 + \\dots \\quad (\\text{even zones blocked}) \\\\ f_m = \\frac{r_1^2}{(2m-1)\\lambda}, \\quad m = 1, 2, 3, \\dots", "body": "Draw concentric circles of radii r1*sqrt(n), blacken alternate rings and photograph at reduced scale. Principle 2 · construction 1.5 · focal length formula 1.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The radii of the concentric circles of a zone plate are proportional to the ____.", "options": ["square roots of natural numbers", "squares of natural numbers", "cubes of natural numbers", "logarithms of natural numbers"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The n-th half-period zone has radius rn = r1 sqrt(n)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Unlike a glass convex lens, a zone plate possesses ____.", "options": ["multiple foci", "a single focus", "zero chromatic aberration", "negative focal length only"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Higher-order foci occur at f1/3, f1/5, f1/7, etc."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The principal focal length \\( f_1 \\) of a zone plate is equal to ____.", "options": ["r1 squared over lambda", "r1 over lambda", "lambda over r1 squared", "2 r1 lambda"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Since r1 = sqrt(f1 lambda), we have f1 = r1^2 / lambda."}
          ]
