          "id": "opt-pyq-n23-q21",
          "title": "Q21 · Reflected waves and reflectivity in thin-film interference (10 marks)",
          "icon": "wave",
          "year": 2023,
          "month": "Nov",
          "unit": 10,
          "units": [10],
          "marks": 10,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2023 Q21",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 10 marks", "title": "Question 21", "marks": 10, "q": "In interference, derive the mathematical expressions for the reflected waves. Derive the rigorous expressions for reflectivity."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Mathematical expressions for reflected waves from a thin film", "options": [{"t": "Reflected amplitudes/waves from top and bottom interfaces with phase difference delta derived", "m": 5}, {"t": "Partial wave expressions without phase difference", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Write the complex or sinusoidal reflected waves from both boundaries of the film."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Rigorous expression for reflectivity R and non-reflecting condition", "options": [{"t": "Resultant reflected amplitude and rigorous reflectivity R derived", "m": 5}, {"t": "Approximate reflectivity without denominator or missing steps", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Combine the reflected waves to obtain the rigorous expression for reflectivity R."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q21 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Reflected wave amplitudes and thin-film reflectivity", "body": "Know first: Interference by division of amplitude and non-reflecting films (10). When a plane wave of amplitude \\( A \\) falls on a dielectric film of thickness \\( d \\) and index \\( n_2 \\) between media \\( n_1 \\) and \\( n_3 \\), the reflections at the two interfaces have amplitude reflection coefficients \\( r_1 = \\frac{n_1 - n_2}{n_1 + n_2} \\) and \\( r_2 = \\frac{n_2 - n_3}{n_2 + n_3} \\) with round-trip phase lag \\( \\delta = \\frac{4\\pi n_2 d\\cos\\theta_2}{\\lambda_0} \\). Summing the reflected waves yields the rigorous reflectivity \\( R = \\frac{r_1^2 + r_2^2 + 2r_1 r_2 \\cos\\delta}{1 + r_1^2 r_2^2 + 2r_1 r_2 \\cos\\delta} \\).", "tex": "R = \\frac{r_1^2 + r_2^2 + 2r_1 r_2 \\cos\\delta}{1 + r_1^2 r_2^2 + 2r_1 r_2 \\cos\\delta}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Derivation of reflected waves and reflectivity", "tex": "r_1 = \\frac{n_1 - n_2}{n_1 + n_2}, \\quad r_2 = \\frac{n_2 - n_3}{n_2 + n_3}, \\quad \\delta = \\frac{4\\pi}{\n\\lambda_0} n_2 d \\cos\\theta_2 \\\\ E_{r1} = r_1 E_0 e^{-i\\omega t}, \\quad E_{r2} = t_1 t'_1 r_2 E_0 e^{-i(\\omega t - \\delta)} \\\\ E_r = E_0 e^{-i\\omega t}\\left[r_1 + t_1 t'_1 r_2 e^{i\\delta} + t_1 t'_1 r_2 (-r_1 r_2 e^{i\\delta}) e^{i\\delta} + \\dots\\right] \\\\ \\text{Using } t_1 t'_1 = 1 - r_1^2: \\quad r = \\frac{E_r}{E_0 e^{-i\\omega t}} = \\frac{r_1 + r_2 e^{i\\delta}}{1 + r_1 r_2 e^{i\\delta}} \\\\ R = |r|^2 = r r^* = \\frac{r_1^2 + r_2^2 + 2r_1 r_2 \\cos\\delta}{1 + r_1^2 r_2^2 + 2r_1 r_2 \\cos\\delta}", "body": "Sum the multiple reflected wave amplitudes using Stokes relations and multiply by the complex conjugate to obtain R. Wave expressions 5 · rigorous reflectivity R 5."},
            {
              "type": "derivation",
              "label": "Derivation",
              "title": "Rigorous reflectivity of a thin film",
              "legend": "Incident wave E0 on film n2 (thickness d) between n1 and n3 producing reflected waves Er1, Er2, ...",
              "setup": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 260 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"65\" width=\"220\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#e8f0fe\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"35\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"115\" stroke=\"#188038\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"115\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#188038\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"185\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"25\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"10\">n1</text><text x=\"25\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"10\">n2 (d)</text><text x=\"25\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"10\">n3</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"10\">Er1</text><text x=\"175\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"10\">Er2</text></svg>",
              "phases": ["Interface coefficients", "Reflected wave series", "Geometric sum", "Reflectivity R = |r|^2"],
              "steps": [
                {"phase": 0, "math": "r_1 = \\frac{n_1 - n_2}{n_1 + n_2}, \\quad r_2 = \\frac{n_2 - n_3}{n_2 + n_3}, \\quad \\delta = \\frac{4\\pi n_2 d\\cos\\theta_2}{\\lambda_0}", "note": "Define amplitude reflection coefficients at both surfaces and round-trip phase delay delta."},
                {"phase": 1, "math": "E_r = E_{\\text{inc}}\\left[r_1 + t_1 t'_1 r_2 e^{i\\delta}\\left(1 - r_1 r_2 e^{i\\delta} + r_1^2 r_2^2 e^{2i\\delta} - \\dots\\right)\\right]", "note": "Write the total reflected wave as a superposition of all partial reflected waves."},
                {"phase": 2, "math": "r = r_1 + \\frac{(1 - r_1^2) r_2 e^{i\\delta}}{1 + r_1 r_2 e^{i\\delta}} = \\frac{r_1 + r_2 e^{i\\delta}}{1 + r_1 r_2 e^{i\\delta}}", "note": "Sum the geometric series and apply t1*t'1 = 1 - r1^2."},
                {"phase": 3, "math": "R = |r|^2 = \\frac{r_1^2 + r_2^2 + 2r_1 r_2 \\cos\\delta}{1 + r_1^2 r_2^2 + 2r_1 r_2 \\cos\\delta}", "note": "Multiply r by its complex conjugate r* to obtain the rigorous reflectivity."}
              ],
              "ask": [
                {"q": "What is the round-trip phase difference \\( \\delta \\) inside the film at normal incidence?", "options": ["4 pi n2 d / lambda0", "2 pi n2 d / lambda0", "pi n2 d / lambda0", "n2 d / lambda0"], "answer": 0, "why": "The extra optical path for one round trip at normal incidence is 2 n2 d."},
                {"q": "Which relation connects the transmission and reflection coefficients at the first interface?", "options": ["t1 t'1 = 1 - r1^2", "t1 t'1 = 1 + r1^2", "t1 + r1 = 0", "t1 = r1^2"], "answer": 0, "why": "By conservation of energy (Stokes relation), t1 t'1 + r1^2 = 1."},
                {"q": "What is the simplified complex reflection amplitude \\( r \\) of the thin film?", "options": ["(r1 + r2 e^{i delta}) / (1 + r1 r2 e^{i delta})", "r1 + r2 e^{i delta}", "r1 r2 e^{i delta}", "(r1 - r2) / (1 + r1 r2)"], "answer": 0, "why": "Combining r1 with the geometric sum yields (r1 + r2 e^{i delta}) / (1 + r1 r2 e^{i delta})."},
                {"q": "When does the reflectivity \\( R \\) vanish for a quarter-wave film (\\( \\cos\\delta = -1 \\))?", "options": ["r1 = r2, so n2 = sqrt(n1 n3)", "r1 = -r2, so n2 = n1 + n3", "r1 = 0", "n2 = n1 / n3"], "answer": 0, "why": "For cos(delta) = -1, R = 0 requires r1 - r2 = 0, which gives n2 = sqrt(n1 n3)."}
              ]
            },
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Thin-film interference is an example of interference by division of ____.", "options": ["amplitude", "wavefront", "frequency", "polarization"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The incident beam is partially reflected and partially transmitted at each boundary."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For a non-reflecting quarter-wave film on glass of index \\( n_3 \\) in air (\\( n_1 = 1 \\)), the film index \\( n_2 \\) should equal ____.", "options": ["square root of n3", "n3 squared", "2 n3", "n3 minus 1"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Zero reflection requires n2 = sqrt(n1 n3) = sqrt(n3)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The minimum optical thickness \\( n_2 d \\) of an anti-reflection coating for wavelength \\( \\lambda_0 \\) is ____.", "options": ["lambda0 divided by 4", "lambda0 divided by 2", "lambda0", "2 lambda0"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "A quarter-wave optical thickness gives a round-trip phase difference of pi."}
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
