            {"type": "score", "title": "Q1 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Laws of reflection", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. First, the incident ray, the reflected ray, and the normal to the reflecting surface at the point of incidence all lie in the same plane. Second, the angle of incidence \\( i \\) is equal to the angle of reflection \\( r \\).", "tex": "i = r"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Minimum optical path condition for reflection", "tex": "\\angle APS = \\angle SPB \\implies i = r", "body": "State the coplanarity condition and the equality of angles of incidence and reflection. First law 1 · second law 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In reflection at a mirror, the angle of incidence equals the ____.", "options": ["angle of reflection", "angle of refraction", "critical angle", "polarizing angle"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Fermat's principle of least path yields i = r."},
