            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 2 marks", "title": "Question 7", "marks": 2, "q": "What do you mean by the resolving power of a grating ? Give an expression for the same explaining the terms involved."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Definition of chromatic resolving power and R = lambda / d lambda = m N", "options": [{"t": "Definition, formula R = lambda / d lambda = m N, and terms m, N, d lambda explained", "m": 2}, {"t": "Only formula or only definition given", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Define resolving power and explain m and N in R = mN."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q7 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Resolving power of a diffraction grating", "body": "Know first: N-slit Fraunhofer diffraction pattern and grating. The resolving power of a grating is its capacity to form separate spectral lines for two very close wavelengths \\( \\lambda \\) and \\( \\lambda + d\\lambda \\), defined as \\( R = \\frac{\\lambda}{d\\lambda} = mN \\). Here \\( d\\lambda \\) is the smallest resolvable wavelength difference, \\( m \\) is the order of diffraction, and \\( N \\) is the total number of ruled lines illuminated on the grating.", "tex": "R = \\frac{\\lambda}{d\\lambda} = mN"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Expression for grating resolving power", "tex": "R = \\frac{\\lambda}{d\\lambda} = mN", "body": "Equate the angular position of the m-th principal maximum of lambda + d lambda to the first adjacent minimum of lambda. Definition 1 · formula & terms 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the first-order spectrum (\\( m = 1 \\)), the resolving power of a grating with \\( N \\) lines is ____.", "options": ["N", "2N", "N squared", "1 over N"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "R = mN = 1 * N = N."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "To increase the resolving power of a grating in a given order, one must increase the ____.", "options": ["total number of illuminated lines N", "slit height", "screen distance", "incident intensity"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "R = mN depends on the total number of rulings N."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the zero-order principal maximum (\\( m = 0 \\)), the resolving power of a grating is ____.", "options": ["zero", "infinite", "equal to N", "unity"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "All wavelengths overlap without dispersion at m = 0."}
          ]
        },
