          "id": "opt-pyq-n22o-q8",
          "title": "Q8 · Huygens wave surfaces in a negative uniaxial crystal (2 marks)",
          "icon": "wave",
          "year": 2022,
          "month": "Nov",
          "unit": 20,
          "units": [20],
          "marks": 2,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2022 (CBCSS) Q8",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 2 marks", "title": "Question 8", "marks": 2, "q": "Give a figure illustrating the Huygens wave surfaces produced by a point source embedded in a negative doubly refracting crystal."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Diagram showing inner sphere (o-ray) and outer ellipsoid (e-ray) touching along optic axis", "options": [{"t": "Clear figure with sphere inside ellipsoid touching along the optic axis and labels", "m": 2}, {"t": "Figure drawn without labels or optic axis", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "For a negative crystal (ne < no, ve > vo), the e-wave ellipsoid lies outside the o-wave sphere."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q8 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Wave surfaces in a negative uniaxial crystal", "body": "Know first: Double refraction and Huygens' explanation. In a negative uniaxial crystal (such as calcite, \\( n_e < n_o \\)), the extraordinary ray travels faster than the ordinary ray perpendicular to the optic axis (\\( v_{re} = c/n_e > v_{ro} = c/n_o \\)). Hence the ellipsoid of revolution (e-wavefront) lies outside the sphere (o-wavefront), and the two surfaces touch each other along the optic axis where \\( v_{re} = v_{ro} = c/n_o \\).", "tex": "n_e < n_o \\implies v_e > v_o \\text{ (ellipsoid outside sphere)}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Semi-axes of negative crystal wave surfaces", "tex": "v_{ro} = \\frac{c}{n_o} \\quad (\\text{inner sphere}) \\\\ v_{re}(\\theta = 0) = \\frac{c}{n_o}, \\quad v_{re}\\left(\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\frac{c}{n_e} > \\frac{c}{n_o} \\quad (\\text{outer ellipsoid})", "body": "Draw an inner circle of radius c/no and an outer ellipse of semi-major axis c/ne touching along the optic axis. Correct geometry 1 · labels (o-ray, e-ray, optic axis) 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a negative uniaxial crystal, the refractive indices satisfy ____.", "options": ["n_e less than n_o", "n_e greater than n_o", "n_e equal to n_o", "n_e equal to zero"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "By definition, n_e - n_o < 0 for a negative crystal."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Perpendicular to the optic axis in a negative crystal, the faster wave is the ____.", "options": ["extraordinary wave", "ordinary wave", "longitudinal wave", "acoustic wave"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Since n_e < n_o, v_e = c/n_e > c/n_o = v_o."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "A classic example of a negative uniaxial doubly refracting crystal is ____.", "options": ["calcite", "quartz", "ice", "sodium chloride"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Calcite has n_o = 1.658 and n_e = 1.486."}
          ]
        },
