            {"type": "eval", "q": "Definition of optical activity and two examples", "options": [{"t": "Rotation of plane of polarization defined and two examples (e.g. quartz, sugar solution) given", "m": 2}, {"t": "Only definition or only examples given", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Define the rotation of the plane of vibration and give two examples."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q9 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Optical activity and examples", "body": "Know first: Production and analysis of polarised light (22). Optical activity is the property of certain crystals and solutions by which they continuously rotate the plane of polarization of linearly polarized light passing through them. Two common examples of optically active substances are quartz crystal (along its optic axis) and aqueous sugar solution (or turpentine).", "tex": "\\phi = \\frac{\\pi}{\\lambda}(n_L - n_R)z"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Rotation angle in optically active medium", "tex": "\\theta = S \\cdot l \\cdot c, \\quad \\phi(z) = \\frac{\\pi}{\\lambda}(n_L - n_R)z", "body": "Define optical rotation of linearly polarized light and name two substances such as quartz and sugar solution. Definition 1 · two examples 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "As linearly polarized light traverses an optically active medium, its plane of polarization ____.", "options": ["rotates continuously", "disappears", "becomes unpolarized", "splits into two beams"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Optical activity rotates the plane of oscillation proportional to path length."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "An example of an optically active liquid solution is ____.", "options": ["sugar solution", "pure water", "liquid nitrogen", "mercury"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Helical sugar molecules rotate the plane of polarization."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The angle of optical rotation is directly proportional to the ____.", "options": ["distance traversed in the medium", "square of the beam diameter", "ambient pressure", "mirror curvature"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Rotation phi is proportional to the path length z."}
          ]
        },
