          "unit": 1,
          "units": [1],
          "marks": 2,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2022 (CBCSS) Q12 · also Nov 2021 (CUCBCSS) Q16",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 2 marks", "title": "Question 12", "marks": 2, "q": "What do you mean by pulse dispersion in optical fiber ?"},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Broadening of light pulses due to transit time differences", "options": [{"t": "Temporal broadening of pulses due to modal/chromatic velocity differences explained", "m": 2}, {"t": "Brief mention of broadening without cause", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Define temporal broadening of optical pulses and state its physical cause."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q12 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Pulse dispersion (broadening) in optical fibers", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. Pulse dispersion is the temporal broadening (spreading in time \\( \\Delta\\tau \\)) of a short light pulse as it propagates along an optical fiber. In a step-index multimode fiber, it arises mainly because rays travelling along different angles (modes) cover different path lengths and arrive at the output at different times, limiting the maximum data rate.", "tex": "\\Delta\\tau = \\tau_{\\max} - \\tau_{\\min} = \\frac{L n_1}{c}\\left(\\frac{n_1 - n_2}{n_2}\\right)"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Intermodal time delay", "tex": "\\tau_{\\min} = \\frac{n_1 L}{c}, \\quad \\tau_{\\max} = \\frac{n_1^2 L}{c n_2} \\\\ \\Delta\\tau = \\frac{n_1 L}{c}\\frac{n_1 - n_2}{n_2}", "body": "Explain temporal pulse spreading and write the transit-time difference between axial and extreme meridional rays. Definition 1 · cause/formula 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Pulse dispersion in a communication fiber causes adjacent digital pulses to ____.", "options": ["broaden and overlap", "become sharper", "increase in frequency", "change polarization"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Temporal spreading makes successive pulses overlap, limiting bandwidth."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a step-index multimode fiber, the fastest ray is the one travelling along the ____.", "options": ["fiber axis", "critical angle path", "cladding surface", "outer jacket"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The axial ray has the shortest geometric path length L."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Intermodal dispersion is completely eliminated by using a ____.", "options": ["single-mode fiber", "thicker core fiber", "step-index multimode fiber", "broadband LED"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "A single-mode fiber supports only one fundamental propagation mode."}
          ]
        },
