          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 5 marks", "title": "Question 14", "marks": 5, "q": "Interference fringes are observed with a biprism of refracting angle 1^\\circ and refractive index 1.5 on a screen 0.8 m from it. If the distance between the source and the biprism is 0.2 m, estimate the fringe width when a light of wavelength 690 nm is used."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Virtual source separation d, total distance D, and fringe width beta", "options": [{"t": "Correct d = 2a(n-1)alpha, D = a+b = 1.0 m, and beta = 0.198 mm (or 1.98 x 10^-4 m)", "m": 5}, {"t": "Correct formulas and method with minor angle conversion slip", "m": 3}, {"t": "Only formulas written", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Convert 1 degree to radians, find d = 2a(n-1)alpha and D = a+b, then compute beta = lambda D / d."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q14 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Fringe width beta = 0.198 mm", "body": "Know first: Fresnel's two-mirror and Fresnel's biprism. With \\( a = 0.2\\text{ m} \\), \\( b = 0.8\\text{ m} \\), \\( D = a + b = 1.0\\text{ m} \\), and \\( \\alpha = 1^\\circ = \\frac{\\pi}{180}\\text{ rad} = 0.01745\\text{ rad} \\), the virtual source separation is \\( d = 2a(n - 1)\\alpha = 2(0.2)(0.5)(0.01745) = 3.49\\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m} \\). The fringe width is \\( \\beta = \\frac{\\lambda D}{d} = \\frac{690\\times 10^{-9}\\times 1.0}{3.49\\times 10^{-3}} = 1.98\\times 10^{-4}\\text{ m} = 0.198\\text{ mm} \\).", "tex": "\\beta = 1.98 \\times 10^{-4}\\text{ m} = 0.198\\text{ mm}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Biprism fringe width calculation", "tex": "\\alpha = 1^\\circ = \\frac{\\pi}{180}\\text{ rad} = 0.01745\\text{ rad}, \\quad a = 0.2\\text{ m}, \\quad b = 0.8\\text{ m} \\\\ d = 2a(n - 1)\\alpha = 2 \\times 0.2 \\times (1.5 - 1) \\times 0.01745 = 3.491 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m} \\\\ D = a + b = 0.2 + 0.8 = 1.0\\text{ m} \\\\ \\beta = \\frac{\\lambda D}{d} = \\frac{690 \\times 10^{-9} \\times 1.0}{3.491 \\times 10^{-3}} = 1.977 \\times 10^{-4}\\text{ m} \\approx 0.198\\text{ mm}", "body": "Convert alpha to radians, find virtual slit separation d and total distance D = a + b, then compute beta. Separation d 2 · D and formula 1.5 · final value 1.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In Fresnel's biprism, the separation \\( d \\) between the two virtual coherent sources is ____.", "options": ["2 a (n - 1) alpha", "a (n - 1) alpha", "2 (a + b) alpha", "n a / alpha"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Each thin prism deviates rays by delta = (n - 1) alpha, separating the virtual images by 2 a delta."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When calculating \\( d = 2a(n - 1)\\alpha \\), the acute prism angle \\( \\alpha \\) must be expressed in ____.", "options": ["radians", "degrees", "centimeters", "dioptres"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The small-angle formula uses angle in radians."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a biprism setup, the total distance \\( D \\) from the virtual sources to the screen equals ____.", "options": ["a plus b", "b minus a", "a times b", "b divided by a"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The virtual sources lie in the plane of the slit at distance a + b from the screen."}
