            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 5 marks", "title": "Question 19", "marks": 5, "q": "A step index fiber has a core of refractive index 1.55 and cladding of refractive index 1.5. Determine the numerical aperture of the fiber. Assume that light enters the fiber from air."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Formula NA = sqrt(n1^2 - n2^2) and numerical result", "options": [{"t": "Formula NA = sqrt(n1^2 - n2^2) and NA = 0.3905 calculated", "m": 5}, {"t": "Correct formula and substitution with minor arithmetic error", "m": 3}, {"t": "Formula only", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Substitute n1 = 1.55 and n2 = 1.5 into NA = sqrt(n1^2 - n2^2)."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q19 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Numerical aperture NA = 0.3905", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. For a step-index optical fiber in air (\\( n_0 = 1 \\)), the numerical aperture is \\( \\text{NA} = \\sqrt{n_1^2 - n_2^2} \\). With \\( n_1 = 1.55 \\) and \\( n_2 = 1.50 \\), \\( \\text{NA} = \\sqrt{1.55^2 - 1.50^2} = \\sqrt{2.4025 - 2.2500} = \\sqrt{0.1525} = 0.3905 \\).", "tex": "\\text{NA} = 0.3905"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of numerical aperture", "tex": "n_1 = 1.55, \\quad n_2 = 1.50, \\quad n_0 = 1 \\\\ \\text{NA} = \\frac{\\sqrt{n_1^2 - n_2^2}}{n_0} = \\sqrt{1.55^2 - 1.50^2} \\\\ \\text{NA} = \\sqrt{2.4025 - 2.2500} = \\sqrt{0.1525} = 0.3905", "body": "Substitute core index n1 = 1.55 and cladding index n2 = 1.50 into the numerical aperture equation. Formula 1.5 · substitution 1.5 · result 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For an optical fiber in air, the numerical aperture is given by ____.", "options": ["square root of (n1^2 - n2^2)", "n1 minus n2", "n1 divided by n2", "n1 squared plus n2 squared"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "NA = sin(theta_a) = sqrt(n1^2 - n2^2)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Numerical aperture is a measure of the optical fiber's ____.", "options": ["light-gathering power", "mechanical tensile strength", "core length", "optical activity"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "A larger NA accepts light over a wider cone of angles."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Total internal reflection inside an optical fiber requires that the core index \\( n_1 \\) be ____.", "options": ["greater than the cladding index n2", "less than the cladding index n2", "equal to the cladding index n2", "negative"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Total internal reflection occurs only when light strikes a rarer medium (n1 > n2)."}
          ]
