          "id": "opt-pyq-n22o-q20",
          "title": "Q20 · Michelson interferometer and circular ring brightness (10 marks)",
          "icon": "wave",
          "year": 2022,
          "month": "Nov",
          "unit": 11,
          "units": [11],
          "marks": 10,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2022 (CBCSS) Q20",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 10 marks", "title": "Question 20", "marks": 10, "q": "Using a suitable figure, discuss the principle, construction and working of a Michelson interferometer. Discuss the condition for obtaining brightness in circular rings."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Principle, neat diagram, construction and compensating plate", "options": [{"t": "Division of amplitude principle, labelled diagram, M1/M2/G1/G2 construction and working explained", "m": 6}, {"t": "Diagram and basic working without compensating plate role", "m": 3.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Draw the Michelson interferometer and explain the roles of beam splitter G1, compensating plate G2, and mirrors M1, M2."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Condition for brightness in circular Haidinger fringes", "options": [{"t": "Path difference 2d cos theta (+ lambda/2) derived and brightness condition stated", "m": 4}, {"t": "Formula stated without derivation", "m": 2}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Derive the path difference between virtual air-film reflections and state the constructive interference condition."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q20 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Michelson interferometer and circular fringes", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). The Michelson interferometer works on division of amplitude: a beam from an extended source is split at \\( 45^\\circ \\) by a half-silvered plate \\( G_1 \\) into two perpendicular beams reflected by mirrors \\( M_1 \\) and \\( M_2 \\), with an identical compensating plate \\( G_2 \\) equalizing glass paths. When \\( M_1 \\) and the virtual image \\( M_2' \\) are parallel and separated by \\( d \\), rays at angle \\( \\theta \\) have geometric path difference \\( 2d\\cos\\theta \\) plus a phase change of \\( \\pi \\) on internal/external reflection, giving bright circular fringes of equal inclination when \\( 2d\\cos\\theta = (2m + 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\) (or \\( 2d\\cos\\theta = m\\lambda \\) for effective phase-compensated path).", "tex": "2d\\cos\\theta + \\frac{\\lambda}{2} = m\\lambda"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Path difference and bright circular ring condition", "tex": "\\Delta_{\\text{geom}} = 2d\\cos\\theta \\\\ \\Delta_{\\text{total}} = 2d\\cos\\theta + \\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\quad (\\text{due to } \\pi \\text{ phase shift at } G_1) \\\\ \\text{Bright circular rings: } 2d\\cos\\theta + \\frac{\\lambda}{2} = m\\lambda \\implies 2d\\cos\\theta = (2m - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2}", "body": "Explain the beam splitter G1, compensating plate G2, and mirrors M1, M2, then derive the circular fringe condition from virtual air film thickness d. Diagram & construction 4 · working 2 · circular ring brightness condition 4."},
            {
              "type": "derivation",
              "label": "Derivation",
              "title": "Circular fringe brightness condition in Michelson interferometer",
              "legend": "Beam splitter G1, compensating plate G2, movable mirror M1 and fixed mirror M2 forming virtual air film d.",
              "setup": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 260 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"25\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"105\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"75\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"125\" y1=\"105\" x2=\"155\" y2=\"75\" stroke=\"#188038\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"90\" y=\"18\" width=\"40\" height=\"6\" fill=\"#555\"/><rect x=\"90\" y=\"32\" width=\"40\" height=\"2\" fill=\"#999\"/><rect x=\"200\" y=\"70\" width=\"6\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#555\"/><text x=\"22\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"10\">Source</text><text x=\"135\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"10\">M1</text><text x=\"135\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"9\">M2' (d)</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"10\">M2</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"10\">G1</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"10\">G2</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"10\">Telescope</text></svg>",
              "phases": ["Amplitude splitting", "Optical path equalization", "Virtual air film", "Brightness condition"],
              "steps": [
