            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In paraxial matrix optics, a ray at any reference plane is specified by its height \\( y \\) and ____.", "options": ["optical direction cosine n theta", "intensity I", "wavelength lambda", "polarization angle"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The 2x1 column vector uses height y and reduced angle n*theta."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When a paraxial ray refracts across a flat interface (\\( R \\to \\infty \\)), its optical direction cosine \\( n\\theta \\) ____.", "options": ["remains unchanged", "doubles", "becomes zero", "reverses sign"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Paraxial Snell's law states n1 theta1 = n2 theta2."}
