            {"type": "score", "title": "Q17 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Acceptance angle and critical angle", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. The acceptance angle \\( \\theta_a \\) of an optical fiber is the maximum angle with the fiber axis at which light incident from air enters the core and undergoes total internal reflection at the core-cladding interface, given by \\( \\sin\\theta_a = \\sqrt{n_1^2 - n_2^2} \\). The critical angle \\( \\theta_c \\) is the angle of incidence in the denser core for which the angle of refraction in the rarer cladding is \\( 90^\\circ \\), given by \\( \\sin\\theta_c = n_2 / n_1 \\).", "tex": "\\sin\\theta_a = \\sqrt{n_1^2 - n_2^2}, \\quad \\sin\\theta_c = \\frac{n_2}{n_1}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Relation between acceptance angle and critical angle", "tex": "\\sin\\theta_c = \\frac{n_2}{n_1} \\\\ n_0\\sin\\theta_a = n_1\\cos\\theta_c = \\sqrt{n_1^2 - n_2^2} \\quad (n_0 = 1)", "body": "State both definitions and their expressions in terms of core index n1 and cladding index n2. Acceptance angle 1 · critical angle 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "At the critical angle of incidence in the core, the refracted ray in the cladding travels at ____.", "options": ["90 degrees to the normal", "0 degrees to the normal", "45 degrees to the normal", "180 degrees to the normal"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "At i = theta_c, the refracted ray grazes the core-cladding interface (r = 90 degrees)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The sine of the acceptance angle of a fiber in air is equal to its ____.", "options": ["numerical aperture", "core diameter", "packing fraction", "specific rotation"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "NA = sin(theta_a) = sqrt(n1^2 - n2^2)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Rays entering an optical fiber at an angle greater than the acceptance angle are ____.", "options": ["lost into the cladding by refraction", "guided without loss", "amplified in the core", "focused at the center"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "They strike the core-cladding boundary at less than the critical angle and refract into the cladding."}
          ]
        }
