            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Equivalent focal length F = 30 cm", "body": "Know first: The thin lens, principal foci and focal length. The equivalent focal length \\( F \\) of two coaxial thin lenses of focal lengths \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\) separated by distance \\( d \\) in air is \\( \\frac{1}{F} = \\frac{1}{f_1} + \\frac{1}{f_2} - \\frac{d}{f_1 f_2} \\). Substituting \\( f_1 = 40\\text{ cm} \\), \\( f_2 = 60\\text{ cm} \\), and \\( d = 20\\text{ cm} \\) gives \\( F = 30\\text{ cm} \\).", "tex": "F = 30\\text{ cm}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Equivalent focal length calculation", "tex": "f_1 = 40\\text{ cm}, \\quad f_2 = 60\\text{ cm}, \\quad d = 20\\text{ cm} \\\\ \\frac{1}{F} = \\frac{1}{f_1} + \\frac{1}{f_2} - \\frac{d}{f_1 f_2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{F} = \\frac{1}{40} + \\frac{1}{60} - \\frac{20}{40 \\times 60} = \\frac{60 + 40 - 20}{2400} = \\frac{80}{2400} = \\frac{1}{30}\\text{ cm}^{-1} \\\\ F = 30\\text{ cm}", "body": "Apply the separated two-lens combination formula and solve for F. Formula 1.5 · substitution 1 · answer with units 1.5."},
