            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 3 marks", "title": "Question 1", "marks": 3, "q": "Explain Fermat's principle of stationary time."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Statement of extremum/stationary optical path and integral expression", "options": [{"t": "Stationary (minimum, maximum or constant) time/optical path stated with integral delta int n ds = 0", "m": 3}, {"t": "Only least time statement without stationary condition or formula", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "State the modern stationary-path form of Fermat's principle and write the optical path integral."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q1 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Fermat's principle of stationary time", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. According to Fermat's principle, out of all possible paths connecting two points \\( A \\) and \\( B \\), a light ray follows the path for which the transit time \\( \\tau = \\frac{1}{c}\\int_A^B n\\,ds \\) (or optical path length \\( \\int_A^B n\\,ds \\)) is stationary (an extremum—minimum, maximum, or constant) with respect to infinitesimal variations of the path.", "tex": "\\delta \\int_A^B n\\,ds = 0"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Transit time and variational condition", "tex": "\\tau = \\frac{1}{c}\\sum_i n_i\\,ds_i = \\frac{1}{c}\\int_A^B n\\,ds \\\\ \\delta\\tau = 0 \\iff \\delta\\int_A^B n\\,ds = 0", "body": "Write the transit time integral in a medium of refractive index n(x,y,z) and equate its first variation to zero. Statement 1.5 · integral condition 1.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the modern statement of Fermat's principle, the optical path length between two points is ____.", "options": ["stationary (an extremum)", "always maximum", "always zero", "imaginary"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The path can be a minimum, a maximum, or stationary (constant for nearby paths)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a homogeneous medium of constant refractive index, Fermat's principle implies that light travels in ____.", "options": ["straight lines", "parabolas", "helices", "circles"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "When n is constant, the shortest optical path is the straight line joining A and B."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The time taken by light to traverse a geometric element \\( ds \\) in a medium of index \\( n \\) is ____.", "options": ["n ds over c", "c ds over n", "n c ds", "ds over (n c)"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Since speed in the medium is v = c/n, dt = ds / (c/n) = n ds / c."}
