            {"type": "score", "title": "Q2 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Principle of superposition of waves", "body": "Know first: Superposition of two sinusoidal waves. When two or more wave trains travel simultaneously through the same region of a linear medium, each wave propagates independently, and the resultant displacement \\( \\mathbf{y} \\) at any point and instant is the vector (or algebraic) sum of the displacements produced by the individual waves acting alone: \\( \\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{y}_1 + \\mathbf{y}_2 + \\dots \\). This principle forms the basis of interference and diffraction.", "tex": "\\mathbf{y}(\\mathbf{r}, t) = \\sum_i \\mathbf{y}_i(\\mathbf{r}, t)"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Linear superposition of wave disturbances", "tex": "y(x,t) = y_1(x,t) + y_2(x,t) + \\dots + y_n(x,t) \\\\ \\text{For two waves in one plane: } y = a_1\\sin(\\omega t + \\phi_1) + a_2\\sin(\\omega t + \\phi_2)", "body": "State the vector/algebraic sum rule and note that it holds because the wave differential equation is linear. Statement 2 · equation & significance 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The principle of superposition holds in media where the wave equation is ____.", "options": ["linear", "nonlinear", "discontinuous", "static"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Any linear combination of solutions of a linear differential equation is also a solution."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "According to the superposition principle, when two waves cross each other, they afterward ____.", "options": ["travel unchanged and independently", "destroy each other permanently", "merge into a single particle", "stop propagating"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Each wave retains its own amplitude, frequency, and direction after passing through the overlap region."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When two crests of equal amplitude \\( a \\) meet in phase, the resultant displacement is ____.", "options": ["2a", "zero", "a", "a squared"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Algebraic addition gives y = a + a = 2a."}
          ]
