            {"type": "score", "title": "Q3 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Coherence time and coherence length", "body": "Know first: Interference of light waves. Coherence time \\( \\tau_c \\) is the average time interval over which a light wave train maintains a predictable sinusoidal phase without random phase jumps; it is inversely proportional to the spectral bandwidth, \\( \\tau_c \\approx 1/\\Delta\\nu \\). Coherence length \\( l_c \\) is the spatial length of this coherent wave train, given by \\( l_c = c\\tau_c = \\frac{c}{\\Delta\\nu} = \\frac{\\lambda^2}{\\Delta\\lambda} \\).", "tex": "\\tau_c \\approx \\frac{1}{\\Delta\\nu}, \\quad l_c = c\\tau_c = \\frac{\\lambda^2}{\\Delta\\lambda}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Relations for temporal coherence", "tex": "\\tau_c \\approx \\frac{1}{\\Delta\\nu} \\\\ l_c = c\\tau_c = \\frac{c}{\\Delta\\nu} = \\frac{\\lambda^2}{\\Delta\\lambda}", "body": "Define coherence time tau_c and coherence length l_c = c * tau_c and relate them to spectral line width Delta lambda. Coherence time 1.5 · coherence length 1.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Coherence length \\( l_c \\) is related to coherence time \\( \\tau_c \\) by ____.", "options": ["l_c = c * tau_c", "l_c = tau_c / c", "l_c = c / tau_c", "l_c = c^2 * tau_c"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Distance travelled by light in time tau_c is c * tau_c."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In terms of wavelength \\( \\lambda \\) and spectral width \\( \\Delta\\lambda \\), coherence length equals ____.", "options": ["lambda squared over Delta lambda", "Delta lambda over lambda", "lambda times Delta lambda", "2 pi lambda"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Since |Delta nu| = c Delta lambda / lambda^2, l_c = c / Delta nu = lambda^2 / Delta lambda."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "A highly monochromatic laser source with a very narrow spectral width \\( \\Delta\\nu \\) has a ____.", "options": ["long coherence length", "zero coherence time", "zero wavelength", "negative refractive index"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Smaller Delta nu yields larger tau_c and longer coherence length l_c."}
          ]
        },
