            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 3 marks", "title": "Question 4", "marks": 3, "q": "Discuss the Rayleigh criterion of resolution."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Statement of central maximum falling on first minimum and dip in resultant intensity", "options": [{"t": "Principal maximum of one coincides with first minimum of the other, with angular limit or intensity dip stated", "m": 3}, {"t": "Partial statement of criterion", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "State Rayleigh's condition for two just-resolved diffraction patterns and give the angular separation."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q4 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Rayleigh's criterion for just-resolved images", "body": "Know first: N-slit Fraunhofer diffraction pattern and grating. According to Lord Rayleigh's criterion, two equally bright point sources or spectral lines are just resolved when the central principal maximum of the diffraction pattern of one falls exactly on the first minimum of the diffraction pattern of the other. At this separation (\\( \\theta_{\\min} = \\frac{1.22\\lambda}{D} \\) for a circular aperture), the resultant intensity curve shows a distinct central dip of about \\( 8/\\pi^2 \\approx 81\\% \\) of either peak.", "tex": "\\theta_{\\min} = \\frac{1.22\\lambda}{D} \\text{ (circular)}, \\quad \\frac{I_{\\text{dip}}}{I_{\\max}} = \\frac{8}{\\pi^2} \\approx 0.81"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Rayleigh condition for slits and circular apertures", "tex": "\\text{Slit / Grating: } \\Delta\\beta = \\pi \\text{ or } \\Delta\\gamma = \\frac{\\pi}{N} \\implies \\frac{I_{\\text{mid}}}{I_{\\max}} = \\frac{8}{\\pi^2} \\approx 0.81 \\\\ \\text{Circular aperture: } \\Delta\\theta_{\\min} = \\frac{1.22\\lambda}{D}", "body": "State the coincidence of the principal maximum of one pattern with the first minimum of the second and note the resulting saddle dip. Criterion 2 · formula/dip 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "At Rayleigh's limit of resolution for two slit patterns, the intensity at the midpoint dip is approximately ____.", "options": ["81 percent of the maximum", "100 percent of the maximum", "zero", "50 percent of the maximum"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "At beta = pi/2, 2 * (sin(pi/2)/(pi/2))^2 = 8 / pi^2 = 0.81."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If the angular separation of two point sources is less than \\( 1.22\\lambda/D \\), the images are ____.", "options": ["not resolved", "well resolved", "infinitely sharp", "polarized"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Separations smaller than the Rayleigh limit merge into a single unresolved peak."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Using shorter-wavelength light in a microscope or telescope makes the limit of resolution \\( \\theta_{\\min} \\) ____.", "options": ["smaller (better resolution)", "larger (poorer resolution)", "infinite", "unchanged"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "theta_min = 1.22 lambda / D is directly proportional to wavelength lambda."}
