            {"type": "score", "title": "Q5 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Reflected Newton's rings maxima and minima", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). For near-normal incidence on a film of refractive index \\( n \\) and thickness \\( t = r^2/(2R) \\), reflection at the lower optically denser plate introduces an extra path difference of \\( \\lambda/2 \\), so \\( \\Delta = 2nt + \\lambda/2 \\). Thus, maxima (bright rings) occur when \\( 2nt = (2m - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\), and minima (dark rings) occur when \\( 2nt = m\\lambda \\) (with \\( m = 0, 1, 2, \\dots \\), making the central spot dark).", "tex": "2nt = (2m-1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\text{ (bright)}, \\quad 2nt = m\\lambda \\text{ (dark)}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Film thickness and ring radius conditions", "tex": "\\Delta = 2nt + \\frac{\\lambda}{2}, \\quad t = \\frac{r^2}{2R} \\\\ \\text{Maxima (bright): } 2nt = (2m - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\implies r_m = \\sqrt{\\frac{(2m - 1)\\lambda R}{2n}} \\\\ \\text{Minima (dark): } 2nt = m\\lambda \\implies r_m = \\sqrt{\\frac{m\\lambda R}{n}}", "body": "State the total path difference including the lambda/2 reflection shift and write the thickness/radius equations for maxima and minima. Path difference 1 · maxima 1 · minima 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the reflected Newton's rings system with an air film, the central spot (\\( t = 0 \\)) is ____.", "options": ["dark", "bright", "red", "absent"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "At t = 0, the path difference is lambda/2 due to reflection at the lower glass surface."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In reflected light, the condition for the \\( m \\)-th dark Newton's ring in an air film (\\( n = 1 \\)) is \\( 2t \\) equal to ____.", "options": ["m lambda", "(2m + 1) lambda / 2", "m lambda / 4", "2 m^2 lambda"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "2t + lambda/2 = (2m+1)lambda/2 simplifies to 2t = m lambda."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The diameter of the \\( m \\)-th dark Newton's ring is proportional to the ____.", "options": ["square root of m", "square of m", "cube of m", "reciprocal of m"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "D_m = 2 sqrt(m lambda R / n) is proportional to sqrt(m)."}
          ]
        },
