            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 3 marks", "title": "Question 7", "marks": 3, "q": "Show a figure illustrating the Huygens wave surfaces produced by a point source embedded in a positive doubly refracting crystal."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Diagram showing outer sphere (o-ray) and inner ellipsoid (e-ray) touching along the optic axis", "options": [{"t": "Neat figure showing ellipsoid inside sphere touching along the optic axis with labels", "m": 3}, {"t": "Figure without labels or reversed surfaces", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "For a positive crystal (ne > no, ve < vo), the e-wave ellipsoid lies inside the o-wave sphere."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q7 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Huygens wave surfaces in a positive uniaxial crystal", "body": "Know first: Double refraction and Huygens' explanation. In a positive uniaxial crystal (such as quartz, \\( n_e > n_o \\)), the velocity of the extraordinary ray perpendicular to the optic axis is less than that of the ordinary ray (\\( v_{re} = c/n_e < v_{ro} = c/n_o \\)). Therefore, the prolate ellipsoid of revolution (e-ray wavefront) lies completely inside the sphere (o-ray wavefront), touching it along the optic axis where \\( v_{re} = v_{ro} = c/n_o \\).", "tex": "n_e > n_o \\implies v_e < v_o \\text{ (ellipsoid inside sphere)}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Radii of o-wave sphere and e-wave ellipsoid", "tex": "v_{ro} = \\frac{c}{n_o} \\quad (\\text{outer sphere}) \\\\ v_{re}(\\theta = 0) = \\frac{c}{n_o}, \\quad v_{re}\\left(\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\frac{c}{n_e} < \\frac{c}{n_o} \\quad (\\text{inner ellipsoid})", "body": "Draw an outer circle of radius c/no and an inner ellipse of semi-minor axis c/ne touching along the optic axis. Diagram 2 · labels & explanation 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a positive uniaxial crystal like quartz, the ellipsoid of revolution lies ____.", "options": ["inside the sphere", "outside the sphere", "tangent at the equator only", "at infinity"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Since n_e > n_o, v_e = c/n_e < c/n_o = v_o perpendicular to the optic axis."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For a positive doubly refracting crystal, the birefringence \\( n_e - n_o \\) is ____.", "options": ["positive", "negative", "zero", "imaginary"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Positive crystals are defined by n_e > n_o."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "An example of a positive uniaxial crystal is ____.", "options": ["quartz", "calcite", "tourmaline", "rock salt"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Quartz has n_o = 1.544 and n_e = 1.553."}
          ]
        },
