          "icon": "wave",
          "year": 2021,
          "month": "Nov",
          "unit": 7,
          "units": [7],
          "marks": 3,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2021 (CBCSS) Q10",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 3 marks", "title": "Question 10", "marks": 3, "q": "Discuss the basic steps in holography."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Two-step process: recording (interference) and reconstruction (diffraction)", "options": [{"t": "Both recording of interference pattern and reconstruction by diffraction explained", "m": 3}, {"t": "Only one step explained", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Explain both the recording step and the reconstruction step."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q10 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Recording and reconstruction in holography", "body": "Know first: Interference of light waves. Holography consists of two basic steps: (1) Recording (construction), where a coherent laser beam is split into a reference wave \\( E_R \\) and an object-scattered wave \\( E_O \\) that interfere on a high-resolution photographic plate to record both amplitude and phase as fringes; and (2) Reconstruction, where the developed hologram is illuminated by the reference beam \\( E_R \\) alone, diffracting light to recreate the original 3D virtual image and a conjugate real image.", "tex": "\\text{Step 1: } I = |E_R + E_O|^2; \\quad \\text{Step 2: } T E_R \\to E_O + E_O^*"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Interference recording and diffraction readout", "tex": "\\text{1. Recording (Interference): } I = |E_R + E_O|^2 = I_R + I_O + E_R^* E_O + E_R E_O^* \\\\ \\text{2. Reconstruction (Diffraction): } E_{\\text{out}} \\propto I \\cdot E_R = (I_R + I_O)E_R + I_R E_O + E_R^2 E_O^*", "body": "Describe the two steps: interference during recording and diffraction during reconstruction. Recording step 1.5 · reconstruction step 1.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The first basic step of holography (recording the hologram) is based on the principle of ____.", "options": ["interference", "polarization", "refraction", "absorption"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The object wave and reference wave interfere on the photographic plate."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The second basic step of holography (reading out the image) is based on the principle of ____.", "options": ["diffraction", "total internal reflection", "double refraction", "dispersion"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The reference wave is diffracted by the recorded fringe pattern."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "During reconstruction, the observer looking through the hologram sees a three-dimensional ____.", "options": ["virtual image", "opaque shadow", "linearly polarized slit", "Newton ring"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The diffracted wave I_R E_O diverges from the original object location."}
          ]
        },
