          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 5 marks", "title": "Question 14", "marks": 5, "q": "Determine the separation between the coherent sources formed by a biprism whose inclined faces make angles of 2^\\circ with its base and the slit is 0.1 m away from the biprism. Given, the refractive index of the material of the prism is 1.5."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Conversion of 2 degrees to radians and calculation of d = 2a(n-1)alpha", "options": [{"t": "Formula d = 2a(n-1)alpha, radian conversion, and d = 3.49 x 10^-3 m (3.49 mm)", "m": 5}, {"t": "Formula and substitution without converting degrees to radians", "m": 3}, {"t": "Formula only", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Convert alpha = 2 degrees to radians and evaluate d = 2a(n-1)alpha."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q14 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Source separation d = 3.49 mm", "body": "Know first: Fresnel's two-mirror and Fresnel's biprism. The separation between the two virtual coherent sources formed by a biprism is \\( d = 2a(n - 1)\\alpha \\). With \\( a = 0.1\\text{ m} \\), \\( n = 1.5 \\), and \\( \\alpha = 2^\\circ = 2 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180}\\text{ rad} = 0.03491\\text{ rad} \\), we obtain \\( d = 2(0.1)(0.5)(0.03491) = 3.491\\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m} = 3.49\\text{ mm} \\).", "tex": "d = 3.49 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m} = 3.49\\text{ mm}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of virtual source separation", "tex": "\\alpha = 2^\\circ = 2 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180}\\text{ rad} = 0.03491\\text{ rad} \\\\ a = 0.1\\text{ m}, \\quad n = 1.5 \\\\ d = 2a(n - 1)\\alpha = 2 \\times 0.1 \\times (1.5 - 1) \\times 0.03491 \\\\ d = 0.1 \\times 0.03491 = 3.491 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m} = 3.49\\text{ mm}", "body": "Convert the refracting angle 2 degrees to radians and substitute into d = 2a(n - 1)alpha. Formula 1.5 · radian conversion 1.5 · result 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Fresnel's biprism produces two coherent virtual sources by ____.", "options": ["refraction through two thin acute prisms", "reflection from a single mirror", "diffraction at a circular hole", "double refraction in calcite"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The two halves of the biprism refract light from a single slit to form two virtual images."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If the distance \\( a \\) between the slit and the biprism is doubled, the separation \\( d \\) between the virtual sources ____.", "options": ["doubles", "halves", "remains constant", "becomes zero"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "d = 2a(n - 1)alpha is directly proportional to a."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For a biprism whose base angles are \\( \\alpha = 2^\\circ \\), the obtuse vertex angle of the prism is ____.", "options": ["176 degrees", "178 degrees", "90 degrees", "180 degrees"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "180 - 2*(2 degrees) = 176 degrees."}
          ]
        },
