            {"type": "eval", "q": "Principal focal length f1 = r1^2 / lambda and higher-order foci fm = f1 / (2m-1)", "options": [{"t": "f1 = 200 cm (2 m) and higher-order foci f2 = 66.7 cm, f3 = 40 cm, ... calculated", "m": 5}, {"t": "Only principal focus f1 = 200 cm calculated", "m": 3.5}, {"t": "Formula only", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Identify r1 = 0.1 cm, calculate principal focus f1 = r1^2 / lambda = 200 cm, and list odd-fraction secondary foci."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q16 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Foci at 200 cm, 66.7 cm, 40 cm, ...", "body": "Know first: Fresnel diffraction and zone plate (15). Comparing \\( r_n = 0.1\\sqrt{n}\\text{ cm} \\) with \\( r_n = \\sqrt{n f_1 \\lambda} \\), the first-zone radius is \\( r_1 = 0.1\\text{ cm} \\). With \\( \\lambda = 5\\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm} \\), the principal focus is at \\( f_1 = \\frac{r_1^2}{\\lambda} = \\frac{0.01}{5\\times 10^{-5}} = 200\\text{ cm} = 2\\text{ m} \\), and the higher-order foci are at \\( f_m = \\frac{f_1}{2m-1} = 200\\text{ cm}, 66.7\\text{ cm}, 40\\text{ cm}, 28.6\\text{ cm}, \\dots \\).", "tex": "f_1 = 200\\text{ cm}, \\; f_2 = 66.7\\text{ cm}, \\; f_3 = 40\\text{ cm}, \\dots"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of principal and secondary foci", "tex": "r_n = 0.1\\sqrt{n}\\text{ cm} \\implies r_1 = 0.1\\text{ cm}, \\quad \\lambda = 5 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm} \\\\ f_1 = \\frac{r_1^2}{\\lambda} = \\frac{(0.1)^2}{5 \\times 10^{-5}} = \\frac{10^{-2}}{5 \\times 10^{-5}} = 200\\text{ cm} = 2.0\\text{ m} \\\\ f_m = \\frac{r_1^2}{(2m - 1)\\lambda} = \\frac{f_1}{2m - 1}, \\quad m = 1, 2, 3, \\dots \\\\ f_1 = 200\\text{ cm}, \\quad f_2 = \\frac{200}{3} = 66.67\\text{ cm}, \\quad f_3 = \\frac{200}{5} = 40\\text{ cm}", "body": "Find r1 from the given expression rn = 0.1 sqrt(n) cm, compute f1 = r1^2 / lambda, and divide by odd integers 3, 5, ... for secondary foci. r1 & f1 3 · secondary foci fm 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The secondary foci of a zone plate of principal focal length \\( f_1 \\) are located at distances ____.", "options": ["f1/3, f1/5, f1/7, ...", "f1/2, f1/4, f1/6, ...", "2f1, 3f1, 4f1, ...", "f1^2, f1^3, ..."], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "When each open zone encompasses 3, 5, 7, ... half-period zones, a weaker focus is formed."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Among all the foci of a zone plate, the most intense focus is at ____.", "options": ["f1", "f1/3", "f1/5", "f1/7"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "At f1 each transparent ring contains a single uncancelled half-period zone."},
