          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 5 marks", "title": "Question 17", "marks": 5, "q": "Determine the thickness of a half-wave plate of quartz for a wavelength 500 nm. Given, the refractive indices of the extra-ordinary and ordinary rays are \\mu_e = 1.553 and \\mu_o = 1.544, respectively."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Formula t = lambda / [2(mu_e - mu_o)] and numerical result", "options": [{"t": "Formula t = lambda / [2(mu_e - mu_o)] and t = 2.778 x 10^-5 m (0.0278 mm) (and QWP = 0.0139 mm for Nov 2020)", "m": 5}, {"t": "Correct formula with arithmetic/unit slip", "m": 3}, {"t": "Formula only", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Substitute lambda = 500 x 10^-9 m and mu_e - mu_o = 0.009 into t = lambda / [2(mu_e - mu_o)]."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q17 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Half-wave plate thickness t = 0.0278 mm (27.8 um)", "body": "Know first: Quarter-wave and half-wave plates (21). The minimum thickness of a half-wave plate is \\( t_{\\text{HWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda}{2(\\mu_e - \\mu_o)} \\). With \\( \\lambda = 500\\text{ nm} = 5\\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} \\) and \\( \\mu_e - \\mu_o = 1.553 - 1.544 = 0.009 \\), we find \\( t_{\\text{HWP}} = \\frac{5\\times 10^{-7}}{2 \\times 0.009} = 2.778\\times 10^{-5}\\text{ m} = 0.0278\\text{ mm} \\) (and for a quarter-wave plate in Nov 2020 Q28, \\( t_{\\text{QWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda}{4(\\mu_e - \\mu_o)} = 1.389\\times 10^{-5}\\text{ m} = 0.0139\\text{ mm} \\)).", "tex": "t_{\\text{HWP}} = 2.78 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ m} = 0.0278\\text{ mm}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of HWP (and QWP) thickness", "tex": "\\lambda = 500\\text{ nm} = 5 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m}, \\quad \\mu_e - \\mu_o = 1.553 - 1.544 = 0.009 \\\\ t_{\\text{HWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda}{2(\\mu_e - \\mu_o)} = \\frac{5 \\times 10^{-7}}{2 \\times 0.009} = 2.778 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ m} = 0.0278\\text{ mm} \\\\ t_{\\text{QWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda}{4(\\mu_e - \\mu_o)} = \\frac{5 \\times 10^{-7}}{4 \\times 0.009} = 1.389 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ m} = 0.0139\\text{ mm}", "body": "Compute the birefringence mu_e - mu_o = 0.009 and divide lambda by 2(mu_e - mu_o). Formula 1.5 · substitution 1.5 · answer with units 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "A half-wave plate introduces an optical path difference between the o-ray and e-ray equal to ____.", "options": ["lambda over 2", "lambda over 4", "lambda", "2 lambda"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "An odd multiple of lambda/2 path difference gives a phase difference of pi."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For the same crystal and wavelength, the thickness of a half-wave plate is ____.", "options": ["twice that of a quarter-wave plate", "half that of a quarter-wave plate", "equal to that of a quarter-wave plate", "four times that of a quarter-wave plate"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "lambda / (2 Delta mu) = 2 * [lambda / (4 Delta mu)]."},
