            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "NA = 0.3775 and acceptance angle = 22.18 degrees", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. With \\( n_1 = 1.45 \\) and \\( n_2 = 1.40 \\), the numerical aperture is \\( \\text{NA} = \\sqrt{n_1^2 - n_2^2} = \\sqrt{1.45^2 - 1.40^2} = \\sqrt{0.1425} = 0.3775 \\). The acceptance angle in air is \\( \\theta_a = \\sin^{-1}(\\text{NA}) = \\sin^{-1}(0.3775) = 22.18^\\circ \\).", "tex": "\\text{NA} = 0.3775, \\quad \\theta_a = 22.18^\\circ"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of NA and theta_a", "tex": "n_1 = 1.45, \\quad n_2 = 1.40 \\\\ \\text{NA} = \\sqrt{n_1^2 - n_2^2} = \\sqrt{1.45^2 - 1.40^2} = \\sqrt{2.1025 - 1.9600} = \\sqrt{0.1425} = 0.3775 \\\\ \\theta_a = \\sin^{-1}(\\text{NA}) = \\sin^{-1}(0.3775) = 22.18^\\circ \\; (0.387\\text{ rad})", "body": "Evaluate NA from the core and cladding refractive indices, then take the inverse sine for acceptance angle. NA calculation 2.5 · acceptance angle 2.5."},
