            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 11 marks", "title": "Question 20", "marks": 11, "q": "Discuss the interference by a plane parallel film when illuminated by a plane wave and obtain the conditions for maxima and minima."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Ray diagram and geometric derivation of path difference 2 n d cos r", "options": [{"t": "Clear ray diagram and derivation of geometric path difference Delta = 2 n d cos r using Snell's law", "m": 6}, {"t": "Diagram with formula stated without full geometric derivation", "m": 3}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Draw the parallel film ray diagram and prove that n(AB + BC) - AD = 2 n d cos r."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Phase shift on reflection and conditions for maxima and minima in reflected and transmitted light", "options": [{"t": "lambda/2 reflection shift explained and both maxima and minima conditions obtained", "m": 5}, {"t": "Conditions stated without explaining phase shift", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Include the Stokes pi phase shift at the denser boundary and state constructive and destructive conditions."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q20 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Plane parallel thin-film interference", "body": "Know first: Interference by division of amplitude and non-reflecting films (10). When a plane wave is incident at angle \\( i \\) on a parallel film of thickness \\( d \\) and refractive index \\( n \\) in air, the geometric path difference between rays reflected from the top and bottom surfaces is \\( \\Delta_{\\text{geom}} = n(AB + BC) - AD = 2nd\\cos r \\), where \\( r \\) is the angle of refraction. Because reflection at the upper air-to-film surface introduces a phase change of \\( \\pi \\) (extra path \\( \\lambda/2 \\)), the effective path difference in reflected light is \\( 2nd\\cos r + \\lambda/2 \\), giving maxima when \\( 2nd\\cos r = (2m - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\) and minima when \\( 2nd\\cos r = m\\lambda \\).", "tex": "2nd\\cos r = (2m-1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\text{ (maxima)}, \\quad 2nd\\cos r = m\\lambda \\text{ (minima)}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Derivation of thin-film path difference and extrema", "tex": "\\Delta_{\\text{geom}} = n(AB + BC) - AD, \\quad AB = BC = \\frac{d}{\\cos r} \\\\ AC = 2d\\tan r, \\quad AD = AC\\sin i = 2d\\tan r \\cdot (n\\sin r) = \\frac{2nd\\sin^2 r}{\\cos r} \\\\ \\Delta_{\\text{geom}} = \\frac{2nd}{\\cos r} - \\frac{2nd\\sin^2 r}{\\cos r} = \\frac{2nd(1 - \\sin^2 r)}{\\cos r} = 2nd\\cos r \\\\ \\text{Reflected total path difference: } \\Delta = 2nd\\cos r + \\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\\\ \\text{Maxima (bright): } 2nd\\cos r = (2m - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2}; \\quad \\text{Minima (dark): } 2nd\\cos r = m\\lambda", "body": "Derive the geometric path difference 2nd cos r using Snell's law sin i = n sin r, add the lambda/2 reflection shift, and equate to m lambda and (2m+1)lambda/2. Diagram & geometry 6 · phase shift & conditions 5."},
            {
              "type": "derivation",
              "label": "Derivation",
              "title": "Interference in a plane parallel thin film",
              "legend": "Ray incident at A splits into reflected ray AR1 and internal ray ABC emerging at C as CR2.",
              "setup": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 260 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"65\" width=\"220\" height=\"55\" fill=\"#e8f0fe\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line x1=\"35\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"15\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#188038\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"125\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#188038\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"215\" y2=\"15\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"104\" y2=\"38\" stroke=\"#555\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/><line x1=\"125\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,2\"/><text x=\"72\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"10\">A</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"10\">B</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"10\">C</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"10\">D</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"10\">d</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"10\">n</text></svg>",
              "phases": ["Optical path difference", "Trigonometric substitution", "Snell's law simplification", "Phase shift & extrema"],
              "steps": [
                {"phase": 0, "math": "\\Delta_{\\text{geom}} = n(AB + BC) - AD", "note": "Drop perpendicular CD from C to ray AR1; beyond CD the two reflected rays travel equal paths."},
                {"phase": 1, "math": "AB = BC = \\frac{d}{\\cos r}, \\quad AC = 2d\\tan r, \\quad AD = AC\\sin i", "note": "Express segments AB, BC, AC, and AD in terms of film thickness d and angles i, r."},
                {"phase": 2, "math": "\\Delta_{\\text{geom}} = \\frac{2nd}{\\cos r} - 2d\\tan r(n\\sin r) = \\frac{2nd(1 - \\sin^2 r)}{\\cos r} = 2nd\\cos r", "note": "Substitute sin i = n sin r by Snell's law and use 1 - sin^2(r) = cos^2(r)."},
                {"phase": 3, "math": "\\Delta = 2nd\\cos r + \\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\implies \\begin{cases} 2nd\\cos r = (2m-1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} & \\text{(maxima)} \\\\ 2nd\\cos r = m\\lambda & \\text{(minima)} \\end{cases}", "note": "Add lambda/2 for reflection at the denser upper surface to obtain the bright and dark conditions."}
              ],
              "ask": [
                {"q": "In the thin-film diagram, what is the length of each internal segment \\( AB \\) and \\( BC \\)?", "options": ["d / cos r", "d cos r", "d sin r", "2 d tan r"], "answer": 0, "why": "In the right triangle of height d and angle r, hypotenuse AB = d / cos r."},
                {"q": "Which law is used to replace \\( \\sin i \\) in \\( AD = 2d\\tan r\\sin i \\)?", "options": ["Snell's law: sin i = n sin r", "Malus's law", "Brewster's law", "Fermat's law of reflection"], "answer": 0, "why": "Refraction from air (n=1) into the film (n) gives sin i = n sin r."},
                {"q": "Why is an extra path difference of \\( \\lambda/2 \\) added in the reflected system?", "options": ["Phase change of pi upon reflection at the denser upper surface", "Absorption inside the film", "Dispersion of white light", "Diffraction at the edges"], "answer": 0, "why": "Reflection at A occurs from an optically denser medium (air to film), whereas at B it occurs from a rarer medium."},
                {"q": "What happens as the film thickness \\( d \\to 0 \\) in reflected light?", "options": ["The film appears completely dark (destructive interference)", "The film appears maximally bright", "Only red light is reflected", "Refraction angle becomes 90 degrees"], "answer": 0, "why": "As d -> 0, Delta -> lambda/2, which is the condition for destructive interference."}
              ]
