            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 1 mark", "title": "Question 7", "marks": 1, "q": "True or False : The light ray incident at an angle of incidence greater than acceptance angle on a step index fiber will be refracted through cladding."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "True/False identification", "options": [{"t": "True", "m": 1}, {"t": "Partial", "m": 0.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "When incidence exceeds theta_a, the internal angle at the core-cladding wall is less than theta_c, so the ray refracts into the cladding."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q7 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "True", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. The statement is True. A light ray entering the fiber core at an angle greater than the acceptance angle \\( \\theta_a \\) strikes the core-cladding boundary at an angle of incidence smaller than the critical angle \\( \\theta_c \\), and is therefore refracted out into the cladding.", "tex": "\\theta_{\\text{in}} > \\theta_a \\implies \\phi < \\theta_c \\implies \\text{refracted into cladding (True)}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Condition for refraction into cladding", "tex": "\\theta_i > \\theta_a \\implies \\theta_r > 90^\\circ - \\theta_c \\implies \\phi = 90^\\circ - \\theta_r < \\theta_c", "body": "State True because rays outside the acceptance cone do not undergo total internal reflection. Answer 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When a ray enters a fiber at an angle smaller than the acceptance angle, at the core-cladding interface it undergoes ____.", "options": ["total internal reflection", "refraction into the cladding", "complete absorption", "double refraction"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Rays inside the acceptance cone hit the wall at angles greater than theta_c."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When a ray enters a fiber at an angle greater than the acceptance angle, its angle of incidence at the core-cladding wall is ____.", "options": ["less than the critical angle", "greater than the critical angle", "equal to 90 degrees", "equal to 180 degrees"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Steeper entry gives a smaller angle of incidence with the normal to the cylindrical wall."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Rays that refract into the cladding of an optical fiber are quickly ____.", "options": ["lost by radiation and absorption", "guided without attenuation", "converted to X-rays", "focused at the axis"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Cladding modes are stripped or lost at the outer coating."}
