          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 1 mark", "title": "Question 10", "marks": 1, "q": "True or False : In a negative uniaxial crystal, velocity of O-ray is less than velocity of E-ray."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "True/False identification", "options": [{"t": "True", "m": 1}, {"t": "Partial", "m": 0.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "In a negative uniaxial crystal (ne < no), v_o = c/no is less than v_e = c/ne (except along the optic axis)."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q10 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "True", "body": "Know first: Double refraction and Huygens' explanation (20). The statement is True. In a negative uniaxial crystal (like calcite), \\( n_e < n_o \\), so the velocity of the ordinary ray \\( v_o = c/n_o \\) is less than the velocity of the extraordinary ray \\( v_e \\) in all directions except along the optic axis.", "tex": "n_e < n_o \\implies v_o < v_e \\quad (\\text{True})"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Velocity inequality in negative crystal", "tex": "n_e < n_o \\implies v_o = \\frac{c}{n_o} < v_e = \\frac{c}{n_e} \\quad (\\text{True})", "body": "State True because n_o > n_e implies v_o < v_e. Answer 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a negative uniaxial crystal, the ordinary refractive index \\( n_o \\) is ____.", "options": ["greater than n_e", "less than n_e", "equal to zero", "negative"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Negative birefringence means n_e - n_o < 0, so n_o > n_e."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a positive uniaxial crystal, the velocity of the O-ray compared to the E-ray (off the optic axis) is ____.", "options": ["greater than the E-ray velocity", "less than the E-ray velocity", "zero", "infinite"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "In a positive crystal n_e > n_o, so v_o = c/n_o > c/n_e = v_e."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The direction in a uniaxial crystal along which \\( v_o = v_e \\) is called the ____.", "options": ["optic axis", "pass-axis", "principal focus", "directrix"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "No double refraction occurs for propagation along the optic axis."}
          ]
        },
