            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 19", "marks": 4, "q": "Describe Fresnel's biprism. Explain how the wavelength of light can be determined with the help of it."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Construction of biprism and formation of virtual coherent sources", "options": [{"t": "Obtuse prism (~179 deg) with base angles ~30', ray diagram, and formation of S1, S2 explained", "m": 2}, {"t": "Description without diagram", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Describe the biprism geometry and draw how it forms two virtual sources S1 and S2."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Measurement of beta, D, and d (displacement method or formula) to find lambda", "options": [{"t": "Formula lambda = beta d / D and measurement of beta, D = a+b, and d = 2a(n-1)alpha or sqrt(d1 d2) explained", "m": 2}, {"t": "Only formula beta = lambda D / d stated", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Explain how beta, D, and d are measured on an optical bench to compute lambda = beta d / D."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q19 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Fresnel's biprism and wavelength measurement", "body": "Know first: Fresnel's two-mirror and Fresnel's biprism. Fresnel's biprism consists of two acute-angled thin prisms joined base-to-base (obtuse angle \\( \\approx 179^\\circ \\), acute base angles \\( \\alpha \\approx 30' \\)). Light from a narrow vertical slit \\( S \\) at distance \\( a \\) is refracted by the two halves to form two virtual coherent sources \\( S_1, S_2 \\) separated by \\( d = 2a(n - 1)\\alpha \\). Measuring the fringe width \\( \\beta \\) with a micrometer eyepiece at distance \\( D = a + b \\) and finding \\( d = \\sqrt{d_1 d_2} \\) by the convex-lens displacement method gives \\( \\lambda = \\frac{\\beta d}{D} \\).", "tex": "\\lambda = \\frac{\\beta d}{D}, \\quad d = 2a(n-1)\\alpha = \\sqrt{d_1 d_2}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Wavelength determination formulas", "tex": "d = 2a(n - 1)\\alpha \\quad \\text{or} \\quad d = \\sqrt{d_1 d_2} \\text{ (conjugate lens positions)} \\\\ D = a + b \\\\ \\beta = \\frac{\\lambda D}{d} \\implies \\lambda = \\frac{\\beta d}{D}", "body": "Draw the biprism ray diagram, write the virtual slit separation d, and explain the measurement of beta, D, and d. Description & diagram 2 · wavelength determination 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The obtuse angle of a standard Fresnel biprism is approximately ____.", "options": ["179 degrees", "90 degrees", "60 degrees", "45 degrees"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Very small base angles (~30') keep the virtual sources close together so fringes are wide."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the displacement method with a convex lens in a biprism experiment, the source separation \\( d \\) equals ____.", "options": ["square root of (d1 d2)", "d1 plus d2", "d1 minus d2", "d1 divided by d2"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Since m1 * m2 = (d1/d)(d2/d) = 1 for conjugate positions, d = sqrt(d1 d2)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In Fresnel's biprism experiment, the central zero-order fringe with white light is ____.", "options": ["bright and white (achromatic)", "dark", "purely violet", "missing"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Both refracted paths traverse equal thicknesses of glass, so all wavelengths arrive in phase at the center."}
          ]
        },
