          "units": [11],
          "marks": 4,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2021 (D 10245) Q20 · also Nov 2022 (D 30197) Q20",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 20", "marks": 4, "q": "With neat diagram, explain Michelson's interferometer. Describe how it can be used to determine the difference in wavelength of two waves."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Neat diagram and explanation of Michelson interferometer", "options": [{"t": "Diagram with M1, M2, G1, G2 and explanation of amplitude division", "m": 2}, {"t": "Explanation without diagram", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Draw the interferometer and explain the roles of G1, G2, M1, and M2."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Determination of wavelength difference Delta lambda = lambda^2 / (2 Delta d)", "options": [{"t": "Discordance/consonance method and derivation of Delta lambda = lambda1 lambda2 / (2 Delta d) approx lambda^2 / (2 Delta d)", "m": 2}, {"t": "Formula stated without derivation", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Use 2 Delta d = m lambda1 = (m+1) lambda2 between successive maximum-contrast positions."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q20 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Michelson interferometer and doublet wavelength difference", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). In a Michelson interferometer, beam splitter \\( G_1 \\) divides the incident beam between mirrors \\( M_1 \\) and \\( M_2 \\). When the source emits two close wavelengths \\( \\lambda_1 \\) and \\( \\lambda_2 \\) (such as the sodium D lines), moving \\( M_1 \\) through a distance \\( \\Delta d \\) between two successive positions of maximum distinctness (or minimum contrast) shifts one pattern by \\( m \\) fringes and the other by \\( m + 1 \\) fringes: \\( 2\\Delta d = m\\lambda_1 = (m+1)\\lambda_2 \\), giving \\( \\Delta\\lambda = \\lambda_1 - \\lambda_2 \\approx \\frac{\\lambda^2}{2\\Delta d} \\).", "tex": "\\Delta\\lambda = \\lambda_1 - \\lambda_2 = \\frac{\\lambda_1 \\lambda_2}{2\\Delta d} \\approx \\frac{\\lambda^2}{2\\Delta d}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Derivation of wavelength difference formula", "tex": "2\\Delta d = m\\lambda_1 = (m + 1)\\lambda_2 \\implies m = \\frac{2\\Delta d}{\\lambda_1}, \\quad m + 1 = \\frac{2\\Delta d}{\\lambda_2} \\\\ (m + 1) - m = 1 = 2\\Delta d\\left(\\frac{1}{\\lambda_2} - \\frac{1}{\\lambda_1}\\right) = \\frac{2\\Delta d(\\lambda_1 - \\lambda_2)}{\\lambda_1 \\lambda_2} \\\\ \\Delta\\lambda = \\lambda_1 - \\lambda_2 = \\frac{\\lambda_{\\text{avg}}^2}{2\\Delta d}", "body": "Explain the interferometer setup with diagram, then equate the mirror displacement 2 Delta d between successive beat maxima to derive Delta lambda. Diagram & setup 2 · Delta lambda derivation 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a Michelson interferometer, the difference between two close wavelengths \\( \\Delta\\lambda \\) is given by ____.", "options": ["lambda^2 / (2 Delta d)", "2 Delta d / lambda^2", "lambda / (2 Delta d)", "2 lambda Delta d"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "From 2 Delta d (Delta lambda / lambda^2) = 1, we get Delta lambda = lambda^2 / (2 Delta d)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Between two successive positions of maximum fringe visibility for a doublet, the number of fringes of \\( \\lambda_2 \\) exceeds that of \\( \\lambda_1 \\) by ____.", "options": ["1", "2", "1/2", "zero"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The faster-oscillating pattern gains exactly one full fringe over the other."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When the maxima of \\( \\lambda_1 \\) fall on the minima of \\( \\lambda_2 \\), the fringe contrast is ____.", "options": ["minimum (washout)", "maximum", "infinite", "colored"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Out-of-step superposition of the two fringe systems produces uniform illumination."}
          ]
        },
