            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 22", "marks": 4, "q": "Draw the intensity distribution curve of Fresnel's diffraction at a straight edge and explain it."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Intensity distribution curve and explanation of shadow and illuminated regions", "options": [{"t": "Neat intensity curve drawn, showing 1/4 intensity at geometric shadow edge, damped oscillations in illuminated region, and monotonic decay into shadow", "m": 4}, {"t": "Curve drawn with partial explanation", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Only qualitative text without curve", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Draw the intensity profile across the geometric shadow boundary and explain both regions."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q22 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Fresnel diffraction at a straight edge", "body": "Know first: Fresnel diffraction by a straight edge (16). When cylindrical waves pass a sharp straight edge, the intensity at the exact boundary of the geometrical shadow is one-fourth of the unobstructed intensity (\\( I = I_0/4 \\), since half the wavefront is blocked). Inside the geometrical shadow, the intensity falls off monotonically and rapidly to zero without any maxima or minima. In the illuminated region above the edge, alternate exposure of odd and even numbers of half-period strips produces parallel bright and dark fringes of decreasing contrast that approach uniform intensity \\( I_0 \\).", "tex": "I_{\\text{edge}} = \\frac{I_0}{4}, \\quad x_n = \\sqrt{\\frac{b(a+b)n\\lambda}{a}}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Half-period strip analysis for straight edge", "tex": "A_{\\text{edge}} = \\frac{A_0}{2} \\implies I_{\\text{edge}} = \\frac{I_0}{4} \\\\ \\text{Illuminated region: } \\begin{cases} \\text{Odd strips exposed } \\to \\text{maxima } (I > I_0) \\\\ \\text{Even strips exposed } \\to \\text{minima } (I < I_0) \\end{cases} \\\\ \\text{Shadow region: } I \\to 0 \\text{ monotonically}", "body": "Sketch I(x) vs position x showing I0/4 at x = 0, monotonic decay for x < 0, and damped oscillations around I0 for x > 0. Intensity curve 2 · explanation of regions 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "At the exact boundary of the geometrical shadow of a straight edge, the light intensity is ____.", "options": ["one-fourth of the unobstructed intensity I0", "equal to I0", "zero", "four times I0"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Half the wavefront is blocked, reducing the amplitude to A0/2 and intensity to I0/4."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Inside the geometrical shadow of a straight edge, the light intensity ____.", "options": ["decreases monotonically to zero without fringes", "oscillates with bright and dark fringes", "remains constant at I0", "increases with distance"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Progressively higher-order half-period strips cancel smoothly without sign reversals."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the illuminated region near a straight edge, the spacing between successive diffraction fringes ____.", "options": ["decreases as we move away from the shadow edge", "increases as we move away from the shadow edge", "is strictly constant", "is infinite"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Fringe positions vary as sqrt(n), so fringes crowd closer together farther from the edge."}
          ]
