          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 23", "marks": 4, "q": "Write brief note on (a) Quarter wave plate ; (b) Half wave plate."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Definition, thickness formula, and uses of Quarter-Wave Plate (QWP)", "options": [{"t": "Path difference lambda/4 (phase pi/2), thickness d = lambda / [4|ne - no|], and use for circular/elliptical polarization stated", "m": 2}, {"t": "Definition without thickness formula", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Define QWP, write its thickness formula, and state its function."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Definition, thickness formula, and uses of Half-Wave Plate (HWP)", "options": [{"t": "Path difference lambda/2 (phase pi), thickness d = lambda / [2|ne - no|], and rotation of polarization plane by 2 theta stated", "m": 2}, {"t": "Definition without thickness formula", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Define HWP, write its thickness formula, and state its effect on polarization."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q23 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Quarter-wave plate (QWP) and half-wave plate (HWP)", "body": "Know first: Quarter-wave and half-wave plates (21). (a) A Quarter-Wave Plate is a doubly refracting crystal plate cut with its optic axis parallel to the surface, of thickness \\( d = \\frac{\\lambda_0}{4|n_o - n_e|} \\), which introduces a path difference of \\( \\lambda_0/4 \\) (phase difference \\( \\pi/2 \\)) between the o-ray and e-ray; it converts linearly polarized light into circularly or elliptically polarized light and vice versa. (b) A Half-Wave Plate has thickness \\( d = \\frac{\\lambda_0}{2|n_o - n_e|} \\), introducing a path difference of \\( \\lambda_0/2 \\) (phase difference \\( \\pi \\)); it rotates the plane of linear polarization by \\( 2\\phi \\) and reverses the handedness of circularly polarized light.", "tex": "d_{\\text{QWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda_0}{4|n_o - n_e|}, \\quad d_{\\text{HWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda_0}{2|n_o - n_e|}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Thickness and phase formulas for wave plates", "tex": "\\text{(a) QWP: } |n_o - n_e|d = (2m + 1)\\frac{\\lambda_0}{4}, \\quad \\Delta\\phi = \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\quad d_{\\min} = \\frac{\\lambda_0}{4|n_o - n_e|} \\\\ \\text{(b) HWP: } |n_o - n_e|d = (2m + 1)\\frac{\\lambda_0}{2}, \\quad \\Delta\\phi = \\pi, \\quad d_{\\min} = \\frac{\\lambda_0}{2|n_o - n_e|}", "body": "State the cut orientation, path/phase difference, minimum thickness formula, and optical applications of both plates. QWP 2 · HWP 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In both quarter-wave and half-wave plates, the crystal is cut with its optic axis ____.", "options": ["parallel to the refracting faces", "perpendicular to the refracting faces", "at 45 degrees to the faces", "along a spiral"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "When the optic axis is parallel to the surface, o- and e-rays travel along the same path at different speeds."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When left-circularly polarized light passes normally through a half-wave plate, it emerges as ____.", "options": ["right-circularly polarized light", "unpolarized light", "linearly polarized light", "zero intensity"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "A phase shift of pi reverses the relative phase of the orthogonal components, inverting handedness."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When linearly polarized light oriented at \\( 45^\\circ \\) to the optic axis passes through a quarter-wave plate, it becomes ____.", "options": ["circularly polarized", "unpolarized", "completely absorbed", "linearly polarized"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Equal orthogonal amplitudes with a pi/2 phase difference produce circularly polarized light."}
          ]
