            {"type": "eval", "q": "Four applications of optical fibers", "options": [{"t": "Four applications (telecommunications, medical endoscopy, fiber sensors, military/avionics/networking) listed", "m": 2}, {"t": "Two applications listed", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "List four distinct applications of optical fibers."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q24 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Necessity of cladding and applications of optical fibers", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. Necessity of cladding: (1) provides a clean, protected dielectric interface of controlled refractive index \\( n_2 < n_1 \\) for total internal reflection; (2) prevents light leakage and crosstalk between adjacent fibers in a bundle; (3) protects the core from surface scratches, moisture, and dust; and (4) keeps \\( n_1 - n_2 \\) small to reduce modal dispersion. Four applications: (1) high-speed long-haul telecommunication and internet links, (2) medical endoscopy and laser surgery, (3) fiber optic sensors (gyroscopes, temperature/strain sensors), and (4) industrial inspection and local area networks.", "tex": "n_2 < n_1 \\text{ (controlled TIR)}, \\quad \\text{Telecom, Endoscopy, Sensors, Networking}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Role of cladding index n2", "tex": "\\theta_c = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{n_2}{n_1}\\right), \\quad \\Delta\\tau \\propto (n_1 - n_2)", "body": "List four reasons why cladding is necessary and four practical applications of optical fibers. Cladding necessity 2 · four applications 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a bundle of optical fibers, the cladding prevents light from leaking from one fiber core into another, a problem known as ____.", "options": ["crosstalk", "double refraction", "chromatic aberration", "optical activity"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Cladding isolates the evanescent field of each core from neighbouring fibers."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Flexible coherent bundles of optical fibers are used in medicine to view internal organs in an instrument called an ____.", "options": ["endoscope", "interferometer", "polarimeter", "spectrometer"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "An endoscope transmits illumination and images through flexible fiber bundles."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "By making the cladding refractive index \\( n_2 \\) only slightly smaller than \\( n_1 \\), the intermodal dispersion is ____.", "options": ["reduced", "made infinite", "converted to X-rays", "unaffected"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Pulse broadening Delta tau is proportional to (n1 - n2)."}
          ]
