            {"type": "eval", "q": "Condition 2nt = lambda/2 for least bright thickness and numerical value", "options": [{"t": "Formula t_min = lambda / (4n) and t_min = 1.028 x 10^-7 m (102.8 nm or 1028 A)", "m": 4}, {"t": "Correct formula with arithmetic/unit slip", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Formula 2nt = (2m-1)lambda/2 only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "For bright reflection at normal incidence (cos r = 1) with m = 1, 2nt = lambda/2 so t = lambda / (4n)."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q27 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Least thickness t = 102.8 nm (1028 A)", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). For constructive interference in reflected light at near-normal incidence (\\( \\cos r = 1 \\)), \\( 2nt = (2m - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\). The least non-zero thickness corresponds to \\( m = 1 \\), giving \\( t_{\\min} = \\frac{\\lambda}{4n} = \\frac{5839\\text{ \\AA}}{4 \\times 1.42} = 1028\\text{ \\AA} = 1.028\\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} \\).", "tex": "t_{\\min} = 1.028 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} = 1028\\text{ \\AA}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Minimum bright film thickness calculation", "tex": "\\lambda = 5839\\text{ \\AA} = 5.839 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m}, \\quad n = 1.42, \\quad \\cos r = 1 \\\\ 2nt\\cos r = (2m - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\\\ \\text{For least thickness } (m = 1): \\quad 2nt_{\\min} = \\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\implies t_{\\min} = \\frac{\\lambda}{4n} \\\\ t_{\\min} = \\frac{5.839 \\times 10^{-7}}{4 \\times 1.42} = 1.028 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} = 102.8\\text{ nm} = 1028\\text{ \\AA}", "body": "Set m = 1 and cos r = 1 in the reflected bright-film condition 2nt cos r = (2m-1)lambda/2. Formula 1.5 · substitution 1 · result with units 1.5."},
