            {"type": "eval", "q": "Radius of curvature R and radius of 30th dark ring r30", "options": [{"t": "R = r20^2 / (20 lambda) = 9.03 m and r30 = r20 sqrt(30/20) = 1.347 x 10^-2 m calculated", "m": 4}, {"t": "Only R or only r30 calculated correctly", "m": 2}, {"t": "Formula r_n = sqrt(n lambda R) only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Use r_n^2 = n lambda R to find R from r_20 and then r_30 = r_20 sqrt(3/2)."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q28 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "R = 9.03 m and r_30 = 1.35 x 10^-2 m", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). The radius of the \\( n \\)-th dark ring in an air film is \\( r_n = \\sqrt{n\\lambda R} \\). From \\( r_{20} = 1.1\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ m} \\) and \\( \\lambda = 670\\times 10^{-9}\\text{ m} \\), the radius of curvature of the lens is \\( R = \\frac{r_{20}^2}{20\\lambda} = 9.03\\text{ m} \\). The radius of the 30th dark ring is \\( r_{30} = r_{20}\\sqrt{\\frac{30}{20}} = 1.347\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ m} \\).", "tex": "R = 9.03\\text{ m}, \\quad r_{30} = 1.347 \\times 10^{-2}\\text{ m}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of R and r_30", "tex": "r_n^2 = n\\lambda R, \\quad n = 20, \\quad r_{20} = 1.1 \\times 10^{-2}\\text{ m}, \\quad \\lambda = 670 \\times 10^{-9}\\text{ m} \\\\ R = \\frac{r_{20}^2}{20\\lambda} = \\frac{(1.1 \\times 10^{-2})^2}{20 \\times 670 \\times 10^{-9}} = \\frac{1.21 \\times 10^{-4}}{1.34 \\times 10^{-5}} = 9.03\\text{ m} \\\\ r_{30} = \\sqrt{30\\lambda R} = r_{20}\\sqrt{\\frac{30}{20}} = 1.1 \\times 10^{-2} \\times \\sqrt{1.5} = 1.347 \\times 10^{-2}\\text{ m}", "body": "Solve r_20^2 = 20 lambda R for R, then scale r_20 by sqrt(30/20) to get r_30. Radius of curvature R 2 · radius r_30 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In an air film, the radius \\( r_n \\) of the \\( n \\)-th dark Newton's ring in reflected light is ____.", "options": ["square root of (n lambda R)", "n lambda R", "square root of (n lambda / R)", "n^2 lambda R"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "From 2t = r_n^2 / R = n lambda, we obtain r_n = sqrt(n lambda R)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The ratio of the radius of the 30th dark ring to that of the 20th dark ring is ____.", "options": ["square root of 1.5", "1.5", "2.25", "square root of 2"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "r30 / r20 = sqrt(30 / 20) = sqrt(1.5)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If a liquid of refractive index \\( \\mu > 1 \\) replaces air in Newton's rings, the ring radii ____.", "options": ["contract by a factor of 1/sqrt(mu)", "expand by a factor of mu", "remain unchanged", "become infinite"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "In a liquid of index mu, r_n = sqrt(n lambda R / mu)."}
