            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 29", "marks": 4, "q": "A plane transmission diffraction grating has 40,000 lines in all with grating element 12.5 \\times 10^{-5} cm. Calculate the maximum resolving power for which it can be used in the range of wavelength 5000 \\AA."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Maximum order m_max <= d / lambda and maximum resolving power R_max = m_max N", "options": [{"t": "m_max = d / lambda = 2 (since sin theta <= 1, m = 2.5 -> 2) and R_max = 2 x 40000 = 80,000", "m": 4}, {"t": "Used non-integer m = 2.5 giving 100,000", "m": 3}, {"t": "Formula R = mN only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Find the largest integer order m_max = floor(d / lambda) = floor(2.5) = 2, then compute R_max = m_max N = 80,000."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q29 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Maximum resolving power R_max = 80,000", "body": "Know first: N-slit Fraunhofer diffraction pattern and grating (14). Since \\( \\sin\\theta \\le 1 \\) in \\( d\\sin\\theta = m\\lambda \\), the maximum possible integer order is \\( m_{\\max} = \\lfloor d/\\lambda \\rfloor \\). With \\( d = 12.5\\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm} \\) and \\( \\lambda = 5000\\text{ \\AA} = 5\\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm} \\), \\( d/\\lambda = 2.5 \\), so the highest observable order is \\( m_{\\max} = 2 \\). With \\( N = 40,000 \\), \\( R_{\\max} = m_{\\max} N = 2 \\times 40,000 = 80,000 \\).", "tex": "m_{\\max} = 2, \\quad R_{\\max} = 80,000"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of m_max and R_max", "tex": "N = 40,000, \\quad d = 12.5 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm}, \\quad \\lambda = 5000\\text{ \\AA} = 5 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm} \\\\ m = \\frac{d\\sin\\theta}{\\lambda} \\le \\frac{d}{\\lambda} = \\frac{12.5 \\times 10^{-5}}{5 \\times 10^{-5}} = 2.5 \\implies m_{\\max} = 2 \\\\ R_{\\max} = m_{\\max} N = 2 \\times 40,000 = 80,000", "body": "Determine the largest integer order m_max from d/lambda = 2.5 and multiply by N = 40,000. Maximum order m_max 2 · R_max 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The maximum possible order of spectrum observable with a grating of element \\( d \\) is the integer part of ____.", "options": ["d divided by lambda", "lambda divided by d", "N times d", "2 pi d"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Because sin(theta) cannot exceed 1, m = d sin(theta) / lambda <= d / lambda."},
