            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The theoretical upper bound on the resolving power of a grating of total width \\( W = N d \\) at normal incidence is ____.", "options": ["W divided by lambda", "W times lambda", "lambda divided by W", "N squared"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "R = mN = (W sin theta) / lambda <= W / lambda."}
