            {"type": "eval", "q": "V-number calculation and number of propagating modes N = V^2 / 2", "options": [{"t": "V = (pi d / lambda) NA = 212.1 and N_modes = V^2 / 2 = 22,500", "m": 4}, {"t": "Used diameter 200 um as radius a in V = 2 pi a NA / lambda, giving 90,000", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Formula N = V^2 / 2 only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Core diameter is d = 2a = 200 um (so radius a = 100 um); compute V = pi d NA / lambda and M = V^2 / 2."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q31 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Number of propagating modes M = 22,500", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. For a step-index fiber of core diameter \\( d = 2a = 200\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} = 2\\times 10^{-4}\\text{ m} \\), \\( \\text{NA} = 0.29 \\), and \\( \\lambda = 859\\text{ nm} \\), the normalized frequency (V-number) is \\( V = \\frac{\\pi d}{\\lambda}\\text{NA} = \\frac{\\pi \\times 2\\times 10^{-4} \\times 0.29}{859\\times 10^{-9}} = 212.13 \\). The number of propagating modes is \\( M \\approx \\frac{V^2}{2} = \\frac{212.13^2}{2} \\approx 22,500 \\).", "tex": "V = 212.13, \\quad M = \\frac{V^2}{2} \\approx 22,500"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "V-number and mode count calculation", "tex": "d = 2a = 200\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} = 2 \\times 10^{-4}\\text{ m}, \\quad \\text{NA} = 0.29, \\quad \\lambda = 859 \\times 10^{-9}\\text{ m} \\\\ V = \\frac{2\\pi a}{\\lambda}\\text{NA} = \\frac{\\pi d}{\\lambda}\\text{NA} = \\frac{3.1416 \\times 2 \\times 10^{-4} \\times 0.29}{859 \\times 10^{-9}} = 212.13 \\\\ M \\approx \\frac{V^2}{2} = \\frac{(212.13)^2}{2} \\approx 22,500\\text{ modes}", "body": "Calculate the V-number using core radius a = 100 um and substitute into M = V^2 / 2. V-number 2 · mode count M 2."},
