            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 10 marks", "title": "Question 35", "marks": 10, "q": "What is the principle of holography ? Describe the recording and reconstruction process in holography with the help of suitable diagrams."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Principle of holography and recording process with diagram", "options": [{"t": "Wavefront recording principle, recording diagram, and interference equation I = |E_R + E_O|^2 derived", "m": 5}, {"t": "Qualitative description without equation or diagram", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Explain how both amplitude and phase are recorded by interfering object and reference beams."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Reconstruction process with diagram and mathematical proof of virtual and real images", "options": [{"t": "Reconstruction diagram and mathematical expansion of T * E_R showing zero-order, virtual image (E_O), and conjugate real image (E_O*)", "m": 5}, {"t": "Diagram and qualitative description without mathematical terms", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Show how illuminating the hologram with E_R diffracts light into the 3D virtual and real images."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q35 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Principle, recording, and reconstruction in holography", "body": "Know first: Interference of light waves. Principle: Holography records the complete wavefront (both amplitude and phase) of light scattered from a 3D object by interfering it with a coherent reference wave, and later reconstructs the wavefront by diffraction. Recording: A laser beam is split into a reference wave \\( E_R = A_R e^{i\\phi_R} \\) and an object wave \\( E_O = A_O e^{i\\phi_O} \\), recording intensity \\( I = A_R^2 + A_O^2 + A_R A_O e^{i(\\phi_O - \\phi_R)} + A_R A_O e^{-i(\\phi_O - \\phi_R)} \\) on a photographic plate. Reconstruction: Illuminating the developed hologram with \\( E_R \\) yields \\( E_{\\text{trans}} \\propto (A_R^2 + A_O^2)E_R + A_R^2 E_O + A_R^2 E_O^* e^{2i\\phi_R} \\), forming a 3D virtual image (\\( E_O \\)) and a conjugate real image (\\( E_O^* \\)).", "tex": "I = |E_R + E_O|^2, \\quad E_{\\text{trans}} \\propto (I_R + I_O)E_R + I_R E_O + E_R^2 E_O^*"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Mathematical theory of recording and reconstruction", "tex": "\\text{Recording: } E_R = A_R e^{i\\phi_R}, \\quad E_O = A_O e^{i\\phi_O} \\\\ I = |E_R + E_O|^2 = A_R^2 + A_O^2 + E_R^* E_O + E_R E_O^* = A_R^2 + A_O^2 + 2A_R A_O\\cos(\\phi_O - \\phi_R) \\\\ \\text{Amplitude transmittance: } T = T_0 - \\beta I \\\\ \\text{Reconstruction with } E_R: \\quad E_{\\text{out}} = T E_R = [T_0 - \\beta(A_R^2 + A_O^2)]E_R - \\beta A_R^2 E_O - \\beta A_R^2 E_O^* e^{2i\\phi_R} \\\\ \\text{Term 2 } (-\\beta A_R^2 E_O): \\text{ 3D virtual image; Term 3 } (-\\beta A_R^2 E_O^* e^{2i\\phi_R}): \\text{ conjugate real image}", "body": "Write the complex amplitudes of the reference and object waves, derive the recorded intensity I, and multiply by ER to identify the reconstructed virtual and real waves. Principle & recording 5 · reconstruction & diagrams 5."},
            {
              "type": "derivation",
              "label": "Derivation",
              "title": "Wavefront recording and reconstruction in holography",
              "legend": "Top: Recording interference of reference wave ER and object wave EO on plate H. Bottom: Reconstruction of virtual and real images.",
              "setup": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 260 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"115\" cy=\"85\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8f0fe\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\"/><line x1=\"122\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#188038\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"30\" width=\"5\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#555\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"135\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"120\" width=\"5\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#555\"/><line x1=\"155\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"135\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,2\"/><line x1=\"155\" y1=\"138\" x2=\"215\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#188038\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line x1=\"115\" y1=\"165\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"142\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"9\">Laser ER</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"9\">Object</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"9\">Plate H</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"9\">Virtual (EO)</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"174\" font-size=\"9\">Real (EO*)</text></svg>",
              "phases": ["Wave superposition", "Recorded intensity", "Readout illumination", "Diffracted wave decomposition"],
              "steps": [
                {"phase": 0, "math": "E_{\\text{total}} = E_R + E_O = A_R e^{i\\phi_R} + A_O e^{i\\phi_O}", "note": "Superpose the coherent reference wave ER and scattered object wave EO at the plate."},
                {"phase": 1, "math": "I = |E_R + E_O|^2 = A_R^2 + A_O^2 + E_R^* E_O + E_R E_O^*", "note": "Compute the recorded intensity containing both amplitude product A_R A_O and phase difference phi_O - phi_R."},
                {"phase": 2, "math": "E_{\\text{trans}} = T E_R = (T_0 - \\beta I) E_R", "note": "Illuminate the developed hologram of transmittance T with the reference beam ER."},
                {"phase": 3, "math": "E_{\\text{trans}} = [T_0 - \\beta(A_R^2 + A_O^2)]E_R - \\beta A_R^2 E_O - \\beta E_R^2 E_O^*", "note": "Separate the transmitted field into the direct beam, the 3D virtual image wave EO, and the conjugate real image wave EO*."}
              ],
              "ask": [
                {"q": "Which term in \\( I = A_R^2 + A_O^2 + 2A_R A_O\\cos(\\phi_O - \\phi_R) \\) preserves the phase information \\( \\phi_O \\)?", "options": ["The interference cross-term 2 A_R A_O cos(phi_O - phi_R)", "A_R^2 alone", "A_O^2 alone", "None of the terms"], "answer": 0, "why": "The cosine interference term encodes the relative phase phi_O - phi_R into fringe positions."},
                {"q": "Why is an off-axis reference beam (Leith-Upatnieks setup) preferred in holography?", "options": ["To angularly separate the virtual image, real image, and zero-order beam", "To eliminate the need for a laser", "To make the plate thicker", "To absorb the object beam"], "answer": 0, "why": "An angle between ER and EO separates the +1, -1, and 0 diffraction orders during readout."},
                {"q": "Which reconstructed wave component forms the orthoscopic 3D virtual image?", "options": ["-beta A_R^2 E_O", "-beta E_R^2 E_O*", "T0 E_R", "A_O^2 E_R"], "answer": 0, "why": "-beta A_R^2 E_O is directly proportional to the original diverging object wave E_O."},
                {"q": "What kind of image is formed by the conjugate wave \\( E_O^* \\)?", "options": ["A real image that can be focused on a screen", "A virtual image behind the laser", "An unpolarized shadow", "A dark ring"], "answer": 0, "why": "The complex conjugate wave E_O* converges to form a real image in front of the hologram."}
              ]
