            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Geometrical path length", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. An optical path \\( \\Delta_{\\text{opt}} = n d \\) is defined as the product of the geometrical path length \\( d \\) traversed by light and the refractive index \\( n \\) of the medium.", "tex": "L_{\\text{op}} = n \\cdot d"},
