            {"type": "score", "title": "Q2 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Translation matrix", "body": "Know first: Refraction and reflection at a single spherical surface. The translation matrix \\( \\mathcal{T} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ d/n & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\) describes a ray travelling in a straight line through distance \\( d \\) in a homogeneous medium of refractive index \\( n \\).", "tex": "\\mathcal{T} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ d/n & 1 \\end{bmatrix}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Translation matrix form", "tex": "\\lambda_2 = \\lambda_1, \\quad y_2 = y_1 + \\frac{d}{n}\\lambda_1 \\implies \\mathcal{T} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ d/n & 1 \\end{bmatrix}", "body": "State 'Translation matrix'. Answer 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Straight-line propagation of a paraxial ray over a distance \\( d \\) is represented by the ____.", "options": ["translation matrix", "refraction matrix", "reflection matrix", "Jones matrix"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The translation matrix updates ray height y while keeping optical direction cosine constant."},
