            {"type": "eval", "q": "True/False identification", "options": [{"t": "True", "m": 1}, {"t": "Partial", "m": 0.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "In the paraxial approximation, refraction at a spherical surface is represented by the 2x2 refraction matrix [[1, -P], [0, 1]]."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q6 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "True", "body": "Know first: Refraction and reflection at a single spherical surface. The statement is True. In paraxial optics, refraction at a spherical surface of radius \\( R \\) between media \\( n_1 \\) and \\( n_2 \\) is characterized by the \\( 2\\times 2 \\) refraction matrix \\( \\mathcal{R} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -P \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\), where \\( P = \\frac{n_2 - n_1}{R} \\).", "tex": "\\mathcal{R} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -\\frac{n_2 - n_1}{R} \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\quad (\\text{True})"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "2x2 spherical refraction matrix", "tex": "\\begin{bmatrix} \\lambda_2 \\\\ y_2 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -P \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} \\lambda_1 \\\\ y_1 \\end{bmatrix} \\quad (\\text{True})", "body": "State True. Answer 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The optical power \\( P \\) of a single spherical refracting surface of radius \\( R \\) separating \\( n_1 \\) and \\( n_2 \\) is ____.", "options": ["(n2 - n1) / R", "(n1 + n2) / R", "R / (n2 - n1)", "n1 n2 R"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "From the Gaussian formula n2/v - n1/u = (n2 - n1)/R, the surface power is P = (n2 - n1)/R."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For a plane refracting interface (\\( R \\to \\infty \\)), the \\( 2\\times 2 \\) refraction matrix becomes the ____.", "options": ["identity matrix [[1, 0], [0, 1]]", "zero matrix", "negative identity", "singular matrix"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "As R -> infinity, P = (n2 - n1)/R -> 0."},
