            {"type": "score", "title": "Q11 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Three fundamental results from Fermat's principle", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. The three fundamental laws of geometrical optics obtained from Fermat's principle are: (1) Rectilinear propagation of light in a homogeneous medium, (2) the laws of reflection (\\( i = r \\) and coplanarity), and (3) Snell's laws of refraction (\\( n_1\\sin\\theta_1 = n_2\\sin\\theta_2 \\) and coplanarity, as well as the Principle of Reversibility of light rays).", "tex": "1.\\; \\text{Rectilinear rays}, \\quad 2.\\; i = r, \\quad 3.\\; n_1\\sin\\theta_1 = n_2\\sin\\theta_2"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Three consequences of delta int n ds = 0", "tex": "\\delta\\int_A^B n\\,ds = 0 \\implies \\begin{cases} 1.\\; n = \\text{const} \\implies \\text{straight-line rays} \\\\ 2.\\; \\text{Mirror} \\implies i = r \\\\ 3.\\; \\text{Interface} \\implies n_1\\sin\\theta_1 = n_2\\sin\\theta_2 \\end{cases}", "body": "List the three results derived from Fermat's extremum condition. Three results 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a homogeneous medium, the path of minimum optical length between two points is a ____.", "options": ["straight line", "circle", "catenary", "cycloid"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "A straight line is the shortest distance between two points in Euclidean space."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Minimizing the optical path \\( n_1 AR + n_2 RB \\) across a plane boundary yields ____.", "options": ["Snell's law of refraction", "Malus's law", "Brewster's law", "Biot's law"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Setting dL_op / dx = 0 gives n1 sin(theta1) = n2 sin(theta2)."},
