            {"type": "score", "title": "Q12 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "2x2 system matrix of an optical system", "body": "Know first: The thin lens, principal foci and focal length. A paraxial ray at any plane is specified by its height \\( y \\) and optical direction cosine \\( \\lambda = n\\alpha \\). Between an input plane \\( RP_1 \\) and output plane \\( RP_2 \\), the coordinates are related by the \\( 2\\times 2 \\) system matrix \\( S = \\begin{bmatrix} b & -a \\\\ -d & c \\end{bmatrix} \\) of determinant \\( bc - ad = 1 \\), formed by multiplying the individual refraction and translation matrices in reverse order: \\( S = M_N \\dots M_2 M_1 \\).", "tex": "\\begin{bmatrix} \\lambda_2 \\\\ y_2 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} b & -a \\\\ -d & c \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} \\lambda_1 \\\\ y_1 \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad bc - ad = 1"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "System matrix relation", "tex": "\\begin{bmatrix} \\lambda_2 \\\\ y_2 \\end{bmatrix} = S \\begin{bmatrix} \\lambda_1 \\\\ y_1 \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad S = \\begin{bmatrix} b & -a \\\\ -d & c \\end{bmatrix} = M_N M_{N-1} \\dots M_1 \\\\ \\det S = bc - ad = 1", "body": "Write the 2x2 matrix equation relating (lambda1, y1) to (lambda2, y2) and note that det(S) = 1. Matrix equation 1 · coordinates & determinant 1."},
