            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When an object is placed between the pole and focus (\\( |u| < |R|/2 \\)) of a concave mirror, the image distance \\( v \\) is ____.", "options": ["positive (virtual image)", "negative (real image)", "zero", "equal to -R"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "1/v = 2/R - 1/u > 0 when |u| < |R|/2 and u, R < 0."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For a virtual image formed by reflection or refraction, Fermat's extremum condition applies to the quantity ____.", "options": ["OS minus SI", "OS multiplied by SI", "OS divided by SI", "zero"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "As shown in Example 3.4 of Ghatak, for diverging rays the virtual path difference OS - SI is stationary."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If an object is placed at the center of curvature (\\( u = R \\)) of a concave mirror, the image is formed at ____.", "options": ["v = R", "v = R/2", "v = infinity", "v = 0"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "1/R + 1/v = 2/R gives 1/v = 1/R, so v = R."}
