            {"type": "score", "title": "Q26 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "r_9 = 0.2258 cm and r_10 = 0.2387 cm", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). The radius of the \\( n \\)-th bright Newton's ring in reflected light (air film, \\( \\mu = 1 \\)) is \\( r_n = \\sqrt{\\frac{(2n - 1)\\lambda R}{2}} \\). With \\( R = 100\\text{ cm} \\) and \\( \\lambda = 6\\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm} \\): for \\( n = 9 \\), \\( r_9 = \\sqrt{8.5 \\times 6\\times 10^{-3}} = \\sqrt{0.051} = 0.2258\\text{ cm} \\); for \\( n = 10 \\), \\( r_{10} = \\sqrt{9.5 \\times 6\\times 10^{-3}} = \\sqrt{0.057} = 0.2387\\text{ cm} \\).", "tex": "r_9 = 0.2258\\text{ cm}, \\quad r_{10} = 0.2387\\text{ cm}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of r_9 and r_10 for bright rings", "tex": "R = 100\\text{ cm}, \\quad \\lambda = 6 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm}, \\quad \\lambda R = 6 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ cm}^2 \\\\ r_n = \\sqrt{\\frac{(2n - 1)\\lambda R}{2}} \\\\ n = 9: \\quad r_9 = \\sqrt{\\frac{17 \\times 6 \\times 10^{-3}}{2}} = \\sqrt{0.051} = 0.2258\\text{ cm} \\\\ n = 10: \\quad r_{10} = \\sqrt{\\frac{19 \\times 6 \\times 10^{-3}}{2}} = \\sqrt{0.057} = 0.2387\\text{ cm}", "body": "Substitute n = 9 and n = 10 into the reflected bright-ring radius formula. Formula 1 · r_9 calculation 1.5 · r_10 calculation 1.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In reflected light, the radius of the \\( n \\)-th bright Newton's ring is proportional to the square root of ____.", "options": ["odd integers (2n - 1)", "even integers 2n", "squares n^2", "cubes n^3"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "2t = (2n - 1) lambda / 2 gives r_n = sqrt((2n - 1) lambda R / 2)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The difference between the squares of the radii of two consecutive bright (or dark) rings \\( r_{n+1}^2 - r_n^2 \\) is ____.", "options": ["lambda R (constant)", "2 n lambda R", "zero", "lambda / R"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "r_{n+1}^2 - r_n^2 = (n + 1/2)lambda R - (n - 1/2)lambda R = lambda R."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If a plano-convex lens of larger radius of curvature \\( R \\) is used, the radii of the Newton's rings ____.", "options": ["increase", "decrease", "become zero", "remain unchanged"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Ring radius r_n is proportional to sqrt(R)."}
