            {"type": "eval", "q": "Calculation of NA, acceptance angle theta_a, and cutoff wavelength lambda_c", "options": [{"t": "NA = 0.1085, theta_a = 6.23 deg, and lambda_c = 2 pi a NA / 2.405 = 1.275 um calculated", "m": 4}, {"t": "Two of the three quantities calculated correctly", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "One quantity or formulas only", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Use NA = sqrt(n1^2 - n2^2), theta_a = sin^-1(NA), and single-mode cutoff V_c = 2.405 = 2 pi a NA / lambda_c."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q29 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "NA = 0.1085, theta_a = 6.23 deg, lambda_c = 1.275 um", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. With \\( n_1 = 1.474 \\), \\( n_2 = 1.470 \\), and \\( a = 4.5\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} \\): (1) \\( \\text{NA} = \\sqrt{n_1^2 - n_2^2} = \\sqrt{0.011776} = 0.1085 \\); (2) acceptance angle \\( \\theta_a = \\sin^{-1}(0.1085) = 6.23^\\circ \\); and (3) single-mode cutoff wavelength (at \\( V_c = 2.405 \\)) is \\( \\lambda_c = \\frac{2\\pi a\\,\\text{NA}}{2.405} = 1.275\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} \\) (\\( 1275\\text{ nm} \\)).", "tex": "\\text{NA} = 0.1085, \\quad \\theta_a = 6.23^\\circ, \\quad \\lambda_c = 1.275\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of NA, theta_a, and cutoff wavelength", "tex": "n_1 = 1.474, \\quad n_2 = 1.470, \\quad a = 4.5 \\times 10^{-6}\\text{ m} \\\\ \\text{NA} = \\sqrt{1.474^2 - 1.470^2} = \\sqrt{2.172676 - 2.160900} = \\sqrt{0.011776} = 0.1085 \\\\ \\theta_a = \\sin^{-1}(0.1085) = 6.23^\\circ \\\\ V_c = \\frac{2\\pi a\\,\\text{NA}}{\\lambda_c} = 2.405 \\implies \\lambda_c = \\frac{2\\pi \\times 4.5 \\times 10^{-6} \\times 0.1085}{2.405} = 1.275 \\times 10^{-6}\\text{ m} = 1.275\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m}", "body": "Compute NA from n1 and n2, find theta_a = sin^-1(NA), and solve V_c = 2.405 for the cutoff wavelength lambda_c. NA 1.5 · acceptance angle 1 · cutoff wavelength 1.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The single-mode cutoff wavelength \\( \\lambda_c \\) of a step-index fiber of core radius \\( a \\) is given by ____.", "options": ["(2 pi a NA) / 2.405", "2.405 / (2 pi a NA)", "2 a NA", "pi a^2 / 2.405"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Setting V = 2 pi a NA / lambda_c = 2.405 gives lambda_c = 2 pi a NA / 2.405."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "A step-index fiber guides only a single mode when the operating wavelength \\( \\lambda \\) is ____.", "options": ["greater than the cutoff wavelength lambda_c", "less than the cutoff wavelength lambda_c", "equal to zero", "in the X-ray region"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "V < 2.405 requires lambda > lambda_c."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For a small core radius \\( a = 4.5\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} \\) and \\( \\text{NA} = 0.1085 \\), the fiber at \\( \\lambda = 1.55\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} \\) operates as a ____.", "options": ["single-mode fiber", "highly multimode fiber", "metallic waveguide", "diffraction grating"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Since 1.55 um > lambda_c (1.275 um), V < 2.405 and the fiber is single-mode."}
          ]
