            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Wedge angle calculation", "tex": "\\beta = \\frac{1\\text{ cm}}{100} = 10^{-2}\\text{ cm}, \\quad \\lambda = 6000\\text{ \\AA} = 6 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm}, \\quad n = 1 \\\\ \\beta = \\frac{\\lambda}{2n\\theta} \\implies \\theta = \\frac{\\lambda}{2\\beta} \\\\ \\theta = \\frac{6 \\times 10^{-5}}{2 \\times 10^{-2}} = 3 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ rad} = 0.1719^\\circ", "body": "Find fringe width beta = 0.01 cm from the fringe density and apply theta = lambda / (2 beta). Fringe width beta 1.5 · formula 1 · wedge angle theta 1.5."},
