            {"type": "score", "title": "Q32 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Michelson interferometer fringe types and standardization of the meter", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). In a Michelson interferometer: (1) Circular Haidinger fringes of equal inclination (\\( 2d\\cos\\theta + \\lambda/2 = m\\lambda \\)) form when \\( M_1 \\) is strictly parallel to the virtual image \\( M_2' \\) (\\( d \\neq 0 \\)); (2) Straight (or curved) Fizeau fringes of equal thickness form when \\( M_1 \\) and \\( M_2' \\) are slightly inclined, enclosing a wedge-shaped air film; (3) White-light fringes form when \\( M_1 \\) intersects \\( M_2' \\) (\\( d = 0 \\)), giving a central dark achromatic fringe flanked by 8–10 coloured fringes. Standardization of the meter: Using the monochromatic red cadmium line (\\( \\lambda = 6438.4696\\text{ \\AA} \\)) and nine stepped Fabry-Perot/Michelson etalons (each double the previous length, aligned via white-light fringes), Michelson counted \\( N = 2L/\\lambda \\) fringes and found \\( 1\\text{ m} = 1,553,163.5\\,\\lambda_{\\text{Cd}} \\).", "tex": "d = \\frac{N\\lambda}{2}, \\quad 1\\text{ m} = 1,553,163.5\\,\\lambda_{\\text{Cd}}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Fringe conditions and meter standardization", "tex": "\\text{1. Circular fringes } (M_1 \\parallel M_2'): \\quad 2d\\cos\\theta + \\frac{\\lambda}{2} = m\\lambda \\\\ \\text{2. Straight wedge fringes } (M_1 \\text{ inclined at } \\alpha \\text{ to } M_2'): \\quad 2x\\alpha + \\frac{\\lambda}{2} = m\\lambda \\\\ \\text{3. White-light fringes } (d = 0): \\quad \\Delta = \\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\text{ for all } \\lambda \\text{ at center (dark central fringe)} \\\\ \\text{4. Meter standardization: } L = \\frac{N\\lambda}{2} \\implies 1\\text{ m} = 1,553,163.5\\,\\lambda_{\\text{Cd}} \\; (\\lambda_{\\text{Cd}} = 6438.4696\\text{ \\AA})", "body": "Describe the interferometer, explain the geometry of M1 and M2' for circular, straight, and white-light fringes, and outline the etalon comparison method for the standard meter. Apparatus & 3 fringe types 6 · meter standardization 4."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a Michelson interferometer, straight localized fringes are observed when mirror \\( M_1 \\) and virtual image \\( M_2' \\) are ____.", "options": ["slightly inclined to form a thin air wedge", "strictly parallel with large d", "removed completely", "perpendicular to each other"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Tilting one mirror creates a wedge-shaped air film that forms straight fringes of equal thickness."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "With white light in a Michelson interferometer (with compensating plate), the central fringe at \\( d = 0 \\) is ____.", "options": ["dark (achromatic)", "pure green", "absent", "infinitely wide"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "At d = 0, the sole phase difference is pi from internal vs external reflection at G1."},
