          "title": "Q1 · Determinant of translation matrix (1 mark)",
          "icon": "wave",
          "year": 2019,
          "month": "Nov",
          "unit": 2,
          "units": [2],
          "marks": 1,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2019 Q1",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 1 mark", "title": "Question 1", "marks": 1, "q": "The determinant of translation matrix is ——————."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Value of determinant", "options": [{"t": "1 (unity)", "m": 1}, {"t": "Partial", "m": 0.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "For T = [[1, 0], [d/n, 1]], det(T) = 1*1 - 0*(d/n) = 1."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q1 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "1 (unity)", "body": "Know first: Refraction and reflection at a single spherical surface. The determinant of the translation matrix \\( \\mathcal{T} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ d/n & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\) is always equal to \\( 1 \\).", "tex": "\\det(\\mathcal{T}) = 1"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Determinant evaluation", "tex": "\\det\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ d/n & 1 \\end{bmatrix} = 1 \\times 1 - 0 \\times \\frac{d}{n} = 1", "body": "State 1. Answer 1."},
