            {"type": "score", "title": "Q9 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "False", "body": "Know first: N-slit Fraunhofer diffraction pattern and grating (14). The statement is False. The angular dispersion of a grating is \\( \\frac{d\\theta}{d\\lambda} = \\frac{m}{d\\cos\\theta} \\), which is inversely proportional to the grating element \\( d = a + b \\). Hence a smaller grating element (more lines per cm) gives larger angular dispersion.", "tex": "\\frac{d\\theta}{d\\lambda} = \\frac{m}{d\\cos\\theta} \\propto \\frac{1}{d} \\quad (\\text{False})"},
