            {"type": "score", "title": "Q11 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Fermat's principle and elliptical reflector", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. Fermat's principle states that a light ray travelling between two points follows a path for which the optical path length (or transit time) is stationary with respect to nearby paths. For an elliptical reflector with foci \\( S_1 \\) and \\( S_2 \\) (Example 3.2), the sum of distances \\( S_1P + S_2P \\) is strictly constant for every point \\( P \\) on the ellipse; hence the transit time is stationary (neither maximum nor minimum, but constant) for all paths, and every ray emitted from focus \\( S_1 \\) reflects through the other focus \\( S_2 \\).", "tex": "S_1 P + S_2 P = \\text{constant} \\implies \\delta(S_1 P + S_2 P) = 0"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Stationary path in an ellipsoidal mirror", "tex": "L_{\\text{op}} = n(S_1 P + S_2 P) = 2na = \\text{constant for all } P \\text{ on ellipse} \\\\ \\implies \\delta L_{\\text{op}} = 0 \\text{ for every point } P", "body": "State Fermat's principle and explain that S1P + S2P = 2a is constant for an ellipse, focusing all rays from S1 at S2. Principle 1 · elliptical reflector 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For any point \\( P \\) on an elliptical mirror with foci \\( S_1 \\) and \\( S_2 \\), the path length \\( S_1P + S_2P \\) is ____.", "options": ["constant (stationary)", "zero", "infinite", "proportional to angle"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "By definition of an ellipse, the sum of focal distances S1P + S2P = 2a is constant."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a pulsed ruby or Nd:YAG laser cavity, an elliptical cylindrical reflector is used so that all light from the flashlamp at one focus concentrates on the ____.", "options": ["laser rod placed at the other focus", "outer wall", "power supply", "exit polarizer"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "As noted in Example 3.2 of Ghatak, an elliptical reflector efficiently couples flashlamp light into the laser rod."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "An elliptical reflector illustrates that Fermat's principle requires the transit time to be ____.", "options": ["stationary (not necessarily a strict minimum)", "always a strict maximum", "always zero", "imaginary"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "All reflection paths from S1 to S2 via the ellipse take the exact same time."}
