          "id": "opt-pyq-n19-q13",
          "title": "Q13 · Constructive and destructive interference conditions for normal incidence on a thin film (2 marks)",
          "icon": "wave",
          "year": 2019,
          "month": "Nov",
          "unit": 10,
          "units": [10, 11],
          "marks": 2,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2019 Q13",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 2 marks", "title": "Question 13", "marks": 2, "q": "For the normal incidence of a parallel light beam on a thin film of refractive index n, state the condition for destructive and constructive interference. Explain."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Conditions for constructive and destructive interference at normal incidence (cos r = 1) with explanation of lambda/2 phase shift", "options": [{"t": "2nd = (2m-1)lambda/2 (constructive) and 2nd = m lambda (destructive) in reflected light with lambda/2 reflection phase shift explained", "m": 2}, {"t": "Formulas stated without explaining the lambda/2 phase change", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "At normal incidence (cos r = 1), include the lambda/2 reflection shift at the upper air-film surface."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q13 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Normal-incidence thin-film interference conditions", "body": "Know first: Interference by division of amplitude and non-reflecting films (10). For normal incidence (\\( i = r = 0, \\cos r = 1 \\)) on a film of thickness \\( d \\) and index \\( n \\) in air, the geometric path difference is \\( 2nd \\) and reflection at the denser top surface adds \\( \\lambda/2 \\), so \\( \\Delta = 2nd + \\lambda/2 \\). Thus, in reflected light, constructive interference occurs when \\( 2nd = (2m - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\) and destructive interference occurs when \\( 2nd = m\\lambda \\) (and vice versa in transmitted light).", "tex": "2nd = (2m-1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\text{ (constructive)}, \\quad 2nd = m\\lambda \\text{ (destructive)}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Reflected and transmitted normal-incidence conditions", "tex": "\\Delta_{\\text{refl}} = 2nd + \\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\implies \\begin{cases} \\text{Constructive: } 2nd = (2m - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\\\ \\text{Destructive: } 2nd = m\\lambda \\end{cases}", "body": "State the effective path difference 2nd + lambda/2 at normal incidence and write the constructive and destructive conditions. Conditions 1 · explanation 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "At normal incidence on a soap film in air, destructive interference in reflected light occurs when \\( 2nd \\) equals ____.", "options": ["m lambda", "(2m - 1) lambda / 2", "(2m + 1) lambda / 4", "lambda / 8"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "2nd + lambda/2 = (2m+1)lambda/2 simplifies to 2nd = m lambda."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "At normal incidence on a thin film in air, constructive interference in transmitted light occurs when \\( 2nd \\) equals ____.", "options": ["m lambda", "(2m - 1) lambda / 2", "lambda / 4", "zero only"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "In transmitted light the twice-reflected ray experiences two internal reflections (zero phase shift), so 2nd = m lambda gives maxima."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When a thin film of index \\( n_2 \\) is coated on a glass substrate of higher index \\( n_3 > n_2 > n_1 \\), a phase shift of \\( \\pi \\) occurs at ____.", "options": ["both top and bottom surfaces", "neither surface", "top surface only", "bottom surface only"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Both reflections (air to film and film to glass) are at optically denser media."}
          ]
        },
