            {"type": "score", "title": "Q14 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Origin of colours in thin films", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). When a thin film (such as an oil slick or soap bubble) is illuminated by an extended white-light source, rays reflected from the upper and lower surfaces interfere with effective path difference \\( \\Delta = 2nd\\cos r + \\lambda/2 \\). Because \\( \\Delta \\) depends on wavelength \\( \\lambda \\), thickness \\( d \\), and inclination \\( r \\), at any point and viewing angle some wavelengths satisfy destructive interference and are absent while others satisfy constructive interference, causing the film to display vivid varying colours.", "tex": "2nd\\cos r = (2m-1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\text{ (reinforced)}, \\quad 2nd\\cos r = m\\lambda \\text{ (cancelled)}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Wavelength-selective interference condition", "tex": "\\Delta = 2nd\\cos r + \\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\\\ \\text{Different } (d, r) \\implies \\text{different } \\lambda \\text{ reinforced/cancelled}", "body": "Explain that white light contains all visible wavelengths and the interference condition selects different colours as thickness d and viewing angle r vary. Mechanism 1 · condition & variation 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The colour seen at a particular point on a thin film changes when the observer moves their eye because the ____.", "options": ["angle of refraction r changes", "film refractive index becomes zero", "speed of light in vacuum changes", "source stops emitting"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Changing the viewing angle changes cos(r) in 2nd cos(r), shifting which wavelength is reinforced."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If a thin film is illuminated by strictly monochromatic sodium light instead of white light, one observes ____.", "options": ["alternating yellow and dark fringes", "a full rainbow of colours", "uniform white light", "no reflection at all"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "A single wavelength produces only bright (yellow) maxima and dark minima."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "At any point on a thin film, the colours seen in reflected light and transmitted light are ____.", "options": ["complementary", "identical", "monochromatic", "ultraviolet"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Wavelengths cancelled in reflection are strongly transmitted."}
          ]
        },
