            {"type": "score", "title": "Q17 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Why thick plates show uniform white instead of colours", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). In a thick glass plate (\\( d \\gg \\lambda \\)), the path difference \\( 2nd\\cos r \\) is very large: (1) it exceeds the short coherence length of white light (\\( \\sim\\text{few }\\mu\\text{m} \\)), and (2) at any point, a large number of closely spaced wavelengths across the entire visible spectrum simultaneously satisfy the constructive condition \\( 2nd\\cos r = (2m-1)\\lambda/2 \\) for high orders \\( m \\). Their superposition blends to give uniform white light to the eye.", "tex": "2nd \\gg l_c, \\quad m = \\frac{2nd}{\\lambda} \\gg 1 \\implies \\text{uniform white}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "High-order spectral overlap in a thick film", "tex": "2nd\\cos r = (2m - 1)\\frac{\\lambda}{2} \\implies \\text{for large } d,\\; \\Delta\\lambda \\approx \\frac{\\lambda^2}{2nd} \\ll \\text{visible range} \\\\ \\implies \\text{many colours overlap at every point } \\to \\text{uniform white}", "body": "Explain that in a thick slab many visible wavelengths simultaneously interfere constructively at high order m (and 2nd exceeds coherence length), mixing to white. Explanation 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a thick glass slab illuminated by white light, interference colours are absent because at every point ____.", "options": ["many visible wavelengths satisfy constructive interference and mix to white", "no light is reflected from the bottom surface", "all light is absorbed", "glass is opaque"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Closely spaced maxima throughout the visible spectrum blend into white."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The coherence length of ordinary white light is of the order of ____.", "options": ["a few micrometers (a few wavelengths)", "several kilometers", "one meter", "infinite"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Broad spectral width Delta lambda ~ 300 nm gives l_c = lambda^2 / Delta lambda ~ 1-2 um."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "To observe Haidinger fringes in a relatively thick plane-parallel plate (such as a Fabry-Perot or Michelson plate), one must use ____.", "options": ["highly monochromatic light", "broadband white light", "uncollimated thermal heat", "a opaque screen"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Monochromatic light has a long coherence length and avoids overlapping of multiple colours."}
          ]
