          "id": "opt-pyq-n19-q20",
          "title": "Q20 · Construction of Fresnel's half-period zones and area of each zone (4 marks)",
          "icon": "wave",
          "year": 2019,
          "month": "Nov",
          "unit": 15,
          "units": [15],
          "marks": 4,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2019 Q20 · also Nov 2018 Q28",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 20", "marks": 4, "q": "Explain the construction of Fresnel's half period zones on a plane wave front. Find the area of each zone."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Construction of concentric half-period zones with path step lambda/2", "options": [{"t": "Diagram and construction of spheres of radii b + n lambda / 2 centered at P intersecting the plane wavefront", "m": 2}, {"t": "Verbal description without diagram", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Explain how spheres of radii b + n lambda / 2 centered at P divide the plane wavefront into annular zones."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Derivation of zone radii rn = sqrt(n b lambda) and proof that zone area = pi b lambda", "options": [{"t": "rn^2 = n b lambda derived and Area = pi(rn^2 - r_{n-1}^2) = pi b lambda proved independent of n", "m": 2}, {"t": "Formula pi b lambda stated without derivation", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Derive r_n^2 = n b lambda and subtract consecutive circle areas to show Area = pi b lambda."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q20 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Fresnel half-period zone construction and area pi b lambda", "body": "Know first: Fresnel diffraction and zone plate (15). From observation point \\( P \\) at perpendicular distance \\( b \\) from a plane wavefront \\( ABCD \\) (pole \\( O \\)), concentric spheres of radii \\( b + \\frac{\\lambda}{2}, b + \\frac{2\\lambda}{2}, \\dots, b + \\frac{n\\lambda}{2} \\) cut the plane in circles of radii \\( r_1, r_2, \\dots, r_n \\). The annular ring between the \\( (n-1) \\)-th and \\( n \\)-th circles is the \\( n \\)-th half-period zone. Since \\( r_n^2 = \\left(b + \\frac{n\\lambda}{2}\\right)^2 - b^2 \\approx nb\\lambda \\), the area of the \\( n \\)-th zone is \\( A_n = \\pi(r_n^2 - r_{n-1}^2) = \\pi b\\lambda \\), which is constant and independent of \\( n \\).", "tex": "r_n = \\sqrt{nb\\lambda}, \\quad \\text{Area}_n = \\pi(r_n^2 - r_{n-1}^2) = \\pi b\\lambda"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Proof that areas of half-period zones are equal", "tex": "r_n^2 = \\left(b + \\frac{n\\lambda}{2}\\right)^2 - b^2 = nb\\lambda + \\frac{n^2\\lambda^2}{4} \\approx nb\\lambda \\quad (\\text{since } \\lambda \\ll b) \\\\ r_{n-1}^2 \\approx (n - 1)b\\lambda \\\\ \\text{Area of } n\\text{-th zone} = \\pi r_n^2 - \\pi r_{n-1}^2 = \\pi nb\\lambda - \\pi(n - 1)b\\lambda = \\pi b\\lambda", "body": "Construct the concentric zones on the plane wavefront and prove that pi(r_n^2 - r_{n-1}^2) = pi b lambda. Construction & diagram 2 · area derivation 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the first-order approximation (\\( \\lambda \\ll b \\)), the area of the \\( n \\)-th Fresnel half-period zone is ____.", "options": ["pi b lambda (independent of n)", "n pi b lambda", "pi b^2 / n", "zero"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "pi r_n^2 - pi r_{n-1}^2 = pi n b lambda - pi(n-1)b lambda = pi b lambda."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If the exact term \\( n^2\\lambda^2/4 \\) is retained in \\( r_n^2 \\), the area of the \\( n \\)-th zone increases slightly with \\( n \\), which is compensated by the ____.", "options": ["increasing distance from P", "decreasing wavelength", "refraction in air", "polarization of light"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The slight increase in area is exactly cancelled by the 1/d_n distance factor."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The point \\( O \\) on the plane wavefront that is nearest to the observation point \\( P \\) is called the ____.", "options": ["pole of the wave with respect to P", "second principal focus", "center of curvature", "Brewster point"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The perpendicular dropped from P to the wavefront meets it at the pole O."}
          ]
