          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 22", "marks": 4, "q": "Discuss the application of the thin film interference phenomenon in reducing the reflectivity of lens surfaces."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Phase condition (quarter-wave thickness d = lambda0 / 4n2) and amplitude condition (n2 = sqrt(n1 n3))", "options": [{"t": "Both phase condition d = lambda0 / (4 n2) and refractive index condition n2 = sqrt(n1 n3) derived and coating material (MgF2) mentioned", "m": 4}, {"t": "Only thickness condition d = lambda / (4n) derived without amplitude condition", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Qualitative description only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Explain both the destructive-phase condition (quarter-wave thickness) and the equal-amplitude condition (n2 = sqrt(n1 n3))."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q22 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Non-reflecting thin films (anti-reflection coatings)", "body": "Know first: Interference by division of amplitude and non-reflecting films (10). To reduce reflection losses at a glass lens surface of index \\( n_3 \\) in air (\\( n_1 = 1 \\)), a transparent dielectric film of intermediate refractive index \\( n_2 \\) (such as \\( \\text{MgF}_2 \\) or cryolite, \\( n_1 < n_2 < n_3 \\)) is deposited on the glass. (1) Phase condition: Since reflections at both interfaces occur at denser media (both have a \\( \\pi \\) phase shift), destructive interference at normal incidence requires \\( 2n_2 d = \\lambda_0/2 \\implies d = \\frac{\\lambda_0}{4n_2} \\). (2) Amplitude condition: Complete cancellation requires equal reflected amplitudes \\( r_1 = r_2 \\), which gives \\( n_2 = \\sqrt{n_1 n_3} = \\sqrt{n_3} \\).", "tex": "d = \\frac{\\lambda_0}{4n_2}, \\quad n_2 = \\sqrt{n_1 n_3} = \\sqrt{n_3}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Derivation of phase and index conditions for non-reflecting film", "tex": "\\text{1. Phase condition }(n_1 < n_2 < n_3\\text{, both reflections shift by }\\pi\\text{):} \\\\ \\Delta = 2n_2 d = (2m + 1)\\frac{\\lambda_0}{2} \\implies d_{\\min} = \\frac{\\lambda_0}{4n_2} \\; (\\delta = \\pi) \\\\ \\text{2. Amplitude condition }(R = 0 \\text{ at } \\cos\\delta = -1): \\\\ r_1 = r_2 \\implies \\frac{n_1 - n_2}{n_1 + n_2} = \\frac{n_2 - n_3}{n_2 + n_3} \\implies n_2^2 = n_1 n_3 \\implies n_2 = \\sqrt{n_1 n_3}", "body": "Derive the quarter-wave optical thickness n2 d = lambda0/4 for destructive phase and equate r1 = r2 to obtain n2 = sqrt(n1 n3). Phase condition 2 · amplitude condition & material 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Why does no net relative phase shift occur from the two reflections in an anti-reflection coating where \\( n_1 < n_2 < n_3 \\)?", "options": ["Both reflections take place at optically denser media (both shift by pi)", "Neither reflection has a phase shift", "The film absorbs one wave", "The light is circularly polarized"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Since n1 < n2 and n2 < n3, both top and bottom reflections undergo a pi phase shift, which cancels in their difference."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Camera lenses coated for the middle of the visible spectrum (yellow-green, \\( \\lambda \\approx 550\\text{ nm} \\)) appear slightly purplish/magenta in reflected light because ____.", "options": ["red and violet at the ends of the spectrum are partially reflected", "the glass is dyed purple", "green light is strongly reflected", "ultraviolet light turns purple"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Zero reflection occurs at 550 nm (green-yellow), leaving weak reflections of extreme red and violet."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For a glass lens of refractive index \\( n_3 = 1.50 \\) in air (\\( n_1 = 1 \\)), the ideal refractive index of a single-layer non-reflecting film is ____.", "options": ["sqrt(1.50) = 1.225", "1.50", "2.25", "0.75"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "n2 = sqrt(1 * 1.50) = 1.225."}
          ]
