          "id": "opt-pyq-n19-q24",
          "title": "Q24 · Theory of holography (4 marks)",
          "icon": "wave",
          "year": 2019,
          "month": "Nov",
          "unit": 7,
          "units": [7],
          "marks": 4,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2019 Q24",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 24", "marks": 4, "q": "Give the theory of Holography."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Mathematical theory of recording (interference) and reconstruction (diffraction)", "options": [{"t": "Recording equation I = |E_R + E_O|^2 and reconstruction equation T * E_R yielding direct, virtual (E_O), and real (E_O*) waves derived", "m": 4}, {"t": "Only qualitative explanation or only recording equation", "m": 2}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Derive the interference intensity recorded on the plate and the transmitted waves during reconstruction."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q24 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Mathematical theory of holography", "body": "Know first: Interference of light waves. Let the coherent reference wave be \\( E_R = A_R e^{i\\phi_R} \\) and the object-scattered wave be \\( E_O = A_O e^{i\\phi_O} \\). During recording, the plate receives intensity \\( I = |E_R + E_O|^2 = A_R^2 + A_O^2 + E_R^* E_O + E_R E_O^* \\). After development, the plate's amplitude transmittance is \\( T = T_0 - \\beta I \\). Illuminating with \\( E_R \\) gives \\( E_{\\text{out}} = T E_R = [T_0 - \\beta(A_R^2 + A_O^2)]E_R - \\beta A_R^2 E_O - \\beta E_R^2 E_O^* \\), where \\( -\\beta A_R^2 E_O \\) reconstructs the 3D virtual image and \\( -\\beta E_R^2 E_O^* \\) forms the conjugate real image.", "tex": "I = A_R^2 + A_O^2 + 2A_R A_O\\cos(\\phi_O - \\phi_R), \\quad E_{\\text{out}} = T E_R"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Recording and readout equations", "tex": "E_R = A_R e^{i\\phi_R}, \\quad E_O = A_O e^{i\\phi_O} \\\\ I = (E_R + E_O)(E_R^* + E_O^*) = A_R^2 + A_O^2 + E_R^* E_O + E_R E_O^* \\\\ T = T_0 - \\beta I \\\\ E_{\\text{out}} = T E_R = [T_0 - \\beta(A_R^2 + A_O^2)]E_R - \\beta A_R^2 E_O - \\beta A_R^2 e^{2i\\phi_R} E_O^*", "body": "Write the complex amplitudes of the reference and object beams, expand I = |E_R + E_O|^2, and multiply T = T0 - beta I by E_R. Recording theory 2 · reconstruction theory 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the theory of holography, the amplitude transmittance \\( T \\) of the developed photographic plate is linearly related to the ____.", "options": ["recorded exposure intensity I", "object mass", "ambient temperature", "refractive index of air"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "In the linear region of the emulsion curve, T = T0 - beta * I."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the expression \\( I = A_R^2 + A_O^2 + E_R^* E_O + E_R E_O^* \\), the term that generates the virtual image upon multiplication by \\( E_R \\) is ____.", "options": ["E_R* E_O", "A_R^2", "A_O^2", "E_R E_O*"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "(E_R* E_O) * E_R = |E_R|^2 E_O = A_R^2 E_O, which is proportional to the original object wave E_O."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In the expression \\( I = A_R^2 + A_O^2 + E_R^* E_O + E_R E_O^* \\), the term that generates the conjugate real image is ____.", "options": ["E_R E_O*", "E_R* E_O", "A_R^2", "A_O^2"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "(E_R E_O*) * E_R = E_R^2 E_O*, which converges to form the real image."}
          ]
        },
