            {"type": "eval", "q": "Air-film thickness t = n lambda / 2 and radius of curvature R = D_n^2 / (4 n lambda)", "options": [{"t": "t10 = 10 lambda / 2 = 3 x 10^-6 m (3 um) and R = D10^2 / (40 lambda) = 0.375 m (37.5 cm) calculated", "m": 4}, {"t": "Only t or only R calculated correctly", "m": 2}, {"t": "Formulas only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "At the 10th dark ring in an air film, 2t = 10 lambda so t = 5 lambda = 3 um, and R = r10^2 / (2t) = D10^2 / (40 lambda) = 0.375 m."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q27 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Film thickness t = 3 um and R = 37.5 cm (0.375 m)", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). For the \\( n = 10 \\)-th dark ring in reflected light in an air film, \\( 2t = n\\lambda \\), so the thickness of the air film at the 10th dark ring is \\( t = \\frac{10 \\times 6\\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m}}{2} = 3\\times 10^{-6}\\text{ m} = 3\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} \\). With diameter \\( D_{10} = 0.3\\text{ cm} = 3\\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m} \\) (radius \\( r_{10} = 1.5\\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m} \\)), the radius of curvature is \\( R = \\frac{r_{10}^2}{2t} = \\frac{D_{10}^2}{4n\\lambda} = 0.375\\text{ m} = 37.5\\text{ cm} \\).", "tex": "t = 3 \\times 10^{-6}\\text{ m}, \\quad R = 0.375\\text{ m} = 37.5\\text{ cm}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of air-film thickness t and lens curvature R", "tex": "n = 10, \\quad \\lambda = 6 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m}, \\quad D_{10} = 0.3\\text{ cm} = 3 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m}, \\quad r_{10} = 1.5 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m} \\\\ \\text{1. Air-film thickness: } 2t = n\\lambda \\implies t = \\frac{10 \\times 6 \\times 10^{-7}}{2} = 3 \\times 10^{-6}\\text{ m} = 3\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} \\\\ \\text{2. Radius of curvature: } R = \\frac{r_{10}^2}{2t} = \\frac{(1.5 \\times 10^{-3})^2}{6 \\times 10^{-6}} = 0.375\\text{ m} = 37.5\\text{ cm}", "body": "Find the air-film thickness from 2t = n lambda and then compute R = r^2 / (2t). Thickness t 2 · radius of curvature R 2."},
