            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 28", "marks": 4, "q": "If the diameter of the pupil of the eye is 2mm, find the minimum separation between two points to be resolved by eye. Given that the distance of the points from the eye is 30m and the points are red in colour with wavelength 6 \\times 10^{-7}m."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Rayleigh angular limit theta = 1.22 lambda / D and linear separation x = L * theta", "options": [{"t": "theta = 1.22 lambda / D = 3.66 x 10^-4 rad and minimum separation x = L * theta = 1.098 x 10^-2 m (1.10 cm)", "m": 4}, {"t": "Only angular separation theta = 3.66 x 10^-4 rad calculated", "m": 2}, {"t": "Formula only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Use x / L = 1.22 lambda / D with D = 2 x 10^-3 m, L = 30 m, and lambda = 6 x 10^-7 m."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q28 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Minimum separation x = 1.098 cm (10.98 mm)", "body": "Know first: Single-slit Fraunhofer diffraction pattern (12). By Rayleigh's criterion for a circular aperture (pupil) of diameter \\( D = 2\\text{ mm} = 2\\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m} \\), the minimum resolvable angular separation is \\( \\theta_{\\min} = \\frac{1.22\\lambda}{D} \\). At distance \\( L = 30\\text{ m} \\) for \\( \\lambda = 6\\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} \\), the minimum linear separation between the two points is \\( x = L\\theta_{\\min} = \\frac{1.22\\lambda L}{D} = 1.098\\times 10^{-2}\\text{ m} = 1.098\\text{ cm} \\).", "tex": "x = \\frac{1.22\\lambda L}{D} = 1.098 \\times 10^{-2}\\text{ m} = 1.098\\text{ cm}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of minimum resolvable separation", "tex": "D = 2\\text{ mm} = 2 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m}, \\quad L = 30\\text{ m}, \\quad \\lambda = 6 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} \\\\ \\theta_{\\min} = \\frac{1.22\\lambda}{D} = \\frac{1.22 \\times 6 \\times 10^{-7}}{2 \\times 10^{-3}} = 3.66 \\times 10^{-4}\\text{ rad} \\\\ x_{\\min} = L\\theta_{\\min} = 30 \\times 3.66 \\times 10^{-4} = 1.098 \\times 10^{-2}\\text{ m} = 1.098\\text{ cm}", "body": "Compute the angular resolution limit 1.22 lambda / D and multiply by the viewing distance L = 30 m. Angular limit 2 · linear separation x 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If two point objects at distance \\( L \\) have linear separation \\( x \\), their angular separation in radians is ____.", "options": ["x divided by L", "L divided by x", "x times L", "x squared L"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "For small angles, theta = x / L."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In dim light when the pupil of the eye dilates (larger \\( D \\)), the theoretical diffraction limit of resolution \\( \\theta_{\\min} = 1.22\\lambda/D \\) ____.", "options": ["decreases (improves)", "increases", "becomes infinite", "becomes negative"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Larger aperture diameter D reduces the diffraction angle 1.22 lambda / D."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For the same pupil diameter \\( D \\), the eye can theoretically resolve closer points in blue light than in red light because blue light has a ____.", "options": ["shorter wavelength", "longer wavelength", "lower frequency", "slower speed in vacuum"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "x_min = 1.22 lambda L / D is smaller for shorter wavelengths."}
