            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 29", "marks": 4, "q": "A zone plate has radii r_n = 0.001\\sqrt{n}m for \\lambda = 4.5 \\times 10^{-7}m, find the positions of foci."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Principal focus f1 = r1^2 / lambda and higher-order foci fm = f1 / (2m-1)", "options": [{"t": "f1 = 10^-6 / (4.5 x 10^-7) = 2.222 m and secondary foci f2 = 0.741 m, f3 = 0.444 m, ... calculated", "m": 4}, {"t": "Only principal focus f1 = 2.22 m calculated", "m": 3}, {"t": "Formula only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Identify r1 = 0.001 m = 10^-3 m, compute f1 = r1^2 / lambda = 2.222 m, and divide by 3, 5, ..."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q29 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Foci at 2.22 m, 0.741 m, 0.444 m, ...", "body": "Know first: Fresnel diffraction and zone plate (15). From \\( r_n = 0.001\\sqrt{n}\\text{ m} \\), the radius of the first zone is \\( r_1 = 10^{-3}\\text{ m} \\). With \\( \\lambda = 4.5\\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} \\), the principal focal length is \\( f_1 = \\frac{r_1^2}{\\lambda} = \\frac{10^{-6}}{4.5\\times 10^{-7}} = 2.222\\text{ m} \\). The higher-order foci lie at \\( f_m = \\frac{f_1}{2m-1} = 2.222\\text{ m}, 0.741\\text{ m}, 0.444\\text{ m}, \\dots \\).", "tex": "f_1 = 2.222\\text{ m}, \\quad f_2 = 0.741\\text{ m}, \\quad f_3 = 0.444\\text{ m}, \\dots"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of zone plate foci", "tex": "r_1 = 0.001\\text{ m} = 10^{-3}\\text{ m}, \\quad \\lambda = 4.5 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} \\\\ f_1 = \\frac{r_1^2}{\\lambda} = \\frac{(10^{-3})^2}{4.5 \\times 10^{-7}} = \\frac{10}{4.5} = 2.222\\text{ m} \\\\ f_m = \\frac{f_1}{2m - 1}: \\quad f_2 = \\frac{2.222}{3} = 0.741\\text{ m}, \\quad f_3 = \\frac{2.222}{5} = 0.444\\text{ m}", "body": "Extract r1 = 10^-3 m, calculate the primary focal length f1 = r1^2 / lambda, and evaluate the odd submultiples. Principal focus f1 2.5 · secondary foci 1.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Why are there no foci at even submultiples \\( f_1/2, f_1/4, \\dots \\) of a standard zone plate?", "options": ["Each open ring contains an even number of half-period zones that mutually cancel", "Refraction blocks even orders", "The wavelength doubles", "Polarization is orthogonal"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "At f1 / (2k), each transparent zone spans 2k half-period zones whose alternating amplitudes cancel in pairs."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "A zone plate also forms virtual foci on the source side at distances ____.", "options": ["-f1, -f1/3, -f1/5, ...", "-2f1, -4f1, ...", "zero", "infinity"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Diffracted rays also diverge as if coming from symmetric virtual foci on the incident side."},
