          "unit": 21,
          "units": [21],
          "marks": 4,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2019 Q30 · also Nov 2022 (D 30197) Q30",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 30", "marks": 4, "q": "Calculate the thickness of double refracting plate capable of producing a path difference of \\lambda/4 between extraordinary and ordinary waves. Given \\lambda = 5500A^0, refractive index of e-ray = 1.54, refractive index of o-ray = 1.53."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Quarter-wave plate formula t = lambda / [4(mu_e - mu_o)] and numerical result", "options": [{"t": "Formula t = lambda / [4(mu_e - mu_o)] and t = 1.375 x 10^-5 m (13.75 um or 0.01375 mm)", "m": 4}, {"t": "Correct formula with unit slip", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Formula only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Substitute lambda = 5.5 x 10^-7 m and mu_e - mu_o = 0.01 into t = lambda / [4(mu_e - mu_o)]."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q30 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Plate thickness t = 1.375 x 10^-5 m (13.75 um)", "body": "Know first: Quarter-wave and half-wave plates (21). A path difference of \\( \\Delta = (\\mu_e - \\mu_o)t = \\frac{\\lambda}{4} \\) requires a plate thickness \\( t = \\frac{\\lambda}{4(\\mu_e - \\mu_o)} \\). Substituting \\( \\lambda = 5500\\text{ \\AA} = 5.5\\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} \\) and \\( \\mu_e - \\mu_o = 1.54 - 1.53 = 0.01 \\) gives \\( t = \\frac{5.5\\times 10^{-7}}{4 \\times 0.01} = 1.375\\times 10^{-5}\\text{ m} = 0.01375\\text{ mm} \\).", "tex": "t = 1.375 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ m} = 13.75\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of quarter-wave plate thickness", "tex": "\\lambda = 5500\\text{ \\AA} = 5.5 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m}, \\quad \\mu_e = 1.54, \\quad \\mu_o = 1.53 \\\\ (\\mu_e - \\mu_o)t = \\frac{\\lambda}{4} \\implies t = \\frac{\\lambda}{4(\\mu_e - \\mu_o)} \\\\ t = \\frac{5.5 \\times 10^{-7}}{4 \\times (1.54 - 1.53)} = \\frac{5.5 \\times 10^{-7}}{0.04} = 1.375 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ m} = 0.01375\\text{ mm}", "body": "Equate the optical path difference (mu_e - mu_o)t to lambda/4 and solve for t. Formula 1.5 · substitution 1 · result with units 1.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "A doubly refracting plate that produces a path difference of \\( \\lambda/4 \\) between the o-ray and e-ray is called a ____.", "options": ["quarter-wave plate", "half-wave plate", "Nicol prism", "zone plate"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "A path difference of lambda/4 (one quarter of a wavelength) defines a quarter-wave plate."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Since \\( \\mu_e = 1.54 \\) is greater than \\( \\mu_o = 1.53 \\), the slower wave inside this crystal plate is the ____.", "options": ["extraordinary wave", "ordinary wave", "incident air wave", "sound wave"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Higher refractive index mu_e gives lower speed v_e = c/mu_e."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If the birefringence \\( |\\mu_e - \\mu_o| \\) of a crystal is larger, the required thickness of a quarter-wave plate is ____.", "options": ["smaller (thinner)", "larger (thicker)", "infinite", "unchanged"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "t = lambda / (4 |mu_e - mu_o|) is inversely proportional to |mu_e - mu_o|."}
          ]
