          "title": "Q31 · Temporal broadening in a step-index fiber after 1 km (4 marks)",
          "icon": "wave",
          "year": 2019,
          "month": "Nov",
          "unit": 1,
          "units": [1],
          "marks": 4,
          "source": "PYQ Nov 2019 Q31",
          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 31", "marks": 4, "q": "For a step index fibre the refractive index of core is 1.50, and refractive index of cladding is 1.48. Calculate the temporal broadening after 1 km. The core radius is such that the ray optics is valid."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Intermodal delay formula Delta tau = (n1 L / c)(n1 - n2)/n2 and numerical value", "options": [{"t": "Formula Delta tau = (n1 L / c)(n1 - n2)/n2 and Delta tau = 6.76 x 10^-8 s (67.6 ns, or 66.7 ns using n1(n1-n2)L/c)", "m": 4}, {"t": "Correct formula with arithmetic/unit slip", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Formula only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Use Delta tau = (n1 L / c)(n1 - n2)/n2 with n1 = 1.50, n2 = 1.48, L = 1000 m, and c = 3 x 10^8 m/s."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q31 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Temporal broadening Delta tau = 67.6 ns", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. In a step-index multimode fiber, the temporal pulse broadening between the axial ray and the extreme critical-angle ray over length \\( L \\) is \\( \\Delta\\tau = \\frac{n_1 L}{c}\\left(\\frac{n_1 - n_2}{n_2}\\right) \\). With \\( n_1 = 1.50 \\), \\( n_2 = 1.48 \\), \\( L = 1\\text{ km} = 10^3\\text{ m} \\), and \\( c = 3\\times 10^8\\text{ m/s} \\), \\( \\Delta\\tau = \\frac{1.50 \\times 10^3}{3\\times 10^8}\\times\\frac{0.02}{1.48} = 6.76\\times 10^{-8}\\text{ s} = 67.6\\text{ ns} \\) (or \\( \\frac{L(n_1 - n_2)}{c} = 66.7\\text{ ns} \\)).", "tex": "\\Delta\\tau = 6.76 \\times 10^{-8}\\text{ s} = 67.6\\text{ ns}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of intermodal temporal broadening", "tex": "n_1 = 1.50, \\quad n_2 = 1.48, \\quad L = 1\\text{ km} = 10^3\\text{ m}, \\quad c = 3 \\times 10^8\\text{ m/s} \\\\ \\tau_{\\min} = \\frac{n_1 L}{c}, \\quad \\tau_{\\max} = \\frac{n_1 L}{c\\sin\\theta_c} = \\frac{n_1^2 L}{c n_2} \\\\ \\Delta\\tau = \\tau_{\\max} - \\tau_{\\min} = \\frac{n_1 L}{c}\\left(\\frac{n_1 - n_2}{n_2}\\right) \\\\ \\Delta\\tau = \\frac{1.50 \\times 10^3}{3 \\times 10^8} \\times \\frac{1.50 - 1.48}{1.48} = 5 \\times 10^{-6} \\times 0.01351 = 6.76 \\times 10^{-8}\\text{ s} = 67.6\\text{ ns}", "body": "Subtract the axial transit time tau_min from the extreme critical-ray transit time tau_max and evaluate for L = 1000 m. Formula 1.5 · substitution 1 · result with units 1.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a step-index multimode fiber of length \\( L \\), the temporal broadening \\( \\Delta\\tau \\) increases ____.", "options": ["linearly with fiber length L", "inversely with L", "as 1 / L^2", "independently of L"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Delta tau = (n1 L / c)(n1 - n2)/n2 is directly proportional to L."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The transit time \\( \\tau_{\\min} \\) of the axial ray over length \\( L \\) in a core of index \\( n_1 \\) is ____.", "options": ["n1 L over c", "c over (n1 L)", "n1 c L", "L over (n1 c)"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Distance L divided by speed c/n1 equals n1 L / c."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For the extreme guided ray striking the core-cladding boundary at the critical angle \\( \\theta_c \\), the geometric path length over fiber length \\( L \\) is ____.", "options": ["L / sin(theta_c) = L n1 / n2", "L sin(theta_c)", "L", "2 L"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The ray makes angle 90 - theta_c with the axis, so path length is L / cos(90 - theta_c) = L / sin(theta_c)."}
          ]
        },
