            {"type": "eval", "q": "Neat labelled ray diagram of Fresnel's double mirror", "options": [{"t": "Diagram showing two plane mirrors M1, M2 inclined at small angle theta, slit S, virtual images S1, S2, and overlapping interference region on screen", "m": 2}, {"t": "Unlabelled or incomplete sketch", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Draw the two nearly coplanar mirrors M1, M2 inclined at small angle theta forming virtual coherent sources S1, S2."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q11 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Fresnel's double-mirror arrangement", "body": "Know first: Fresnel's two-mirror and Fresnel's biprism (8). Fresnel's two-mirror arrangement consists of two optically flat plane mirrors \\( M_1 \\) and \\( M_2 \\) inclined to each other at a very small angle \\( \\theta \\) (almost \\( 180^\\circ \\)) touching along a common edge \\( O \\). Light from a narrow slit \\( S \\) at distance \\( a \\) from \\( O \\) reflects from both mirrors to form two virtual coherent sources \\( S_1 \\) and \\( S_2 \\) separated by \\( d = 2a\\theta \\), producing interference fringes of width \\( \\beta = \\frac{\\lambda(a+b)}{2a\\theta} \\) in the overlap region on a screen at distance \\( b \\) from \\( O \\).", "tex": "d = 2a\\theta, \\quad \\beta = \\frac{\\lambda(a+b)}{2a\\theta}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Geometry of Fresnel's two-mirror interference", "tex": "OS_1 = OS_2 = OS = a, \\quad \\angle S_1 O S_2 = 2\\theta \\\\ d = S_1 S_2 = 2a\\sin\\theta \\approx 2a\\theta \\\\ D = a + b \\implies \\beta = \\frac{\\lambda D}{d} = \\frac{\\lambda(a + b)}{2a\\theta}", "body": "Draw the two inclined mirrors M1, M2, source S, virtual images S1, S2 on the circle of radius a, and the screen. Diagram 1.5 · labels/formula 0.5."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In Fresnel's double mirror, if the two mirrors are inclined at a small angle \\( \\theta \\) and the slit is at distance \\( a \\) from their intersection line, the angle subtended by the two virtual images \\( S_1, S_2 \\) at the intersection is ____.", "options": ["2 theta", "theta", "theta over 2", "90 degrees"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Rotating a mirror by angle theta rotates the reflected ray and virtual image by 2 theta."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In Fresnel's two-mirror experiment, the distance \\( d \\) between the two virtual coherent sources is ____.", "options": ["2 a theta", "a theta", "2 a (n - 1) theta", "a / theta"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Chord length on a circle of radius a subtending angle 2 theta is 2 a sin(theta) ~ 2 a theta."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Fresnel's double mirror proved that interference fringes can be produced by reflection alone without any ____.", "options": ["diffraction at slit edges or refraction in prisms", "coherent source", "screen", "light wave"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Fresnel designed the double mirror to counter objections that Young's fringes were merely edge-diffraction effects."}
