            {"type": "score", "title": "Q15 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Comparison between a zone plate and a convex lens", "body": "Know first: Fresnel diffraction and zone plate (15). Similarity: Both form real and virtual images and obey the conjugate distance relation \\( \\frac{1}{v} + \\frac{1}{u} = \\frac{1}{f} \\). Differences: (1) A convex lens works by refraction and has a single focus where all rays arrive with the same optical path, whereas a zone plate works by diffraction and has multiple real and virtual foci \\( f_m = \\frac{r_1^2}{(2m-1)\\lambda} \\); (2) for a zone plate \\( f = r_1^2/\\lambda \\) so \\( f_{\\text{red}} < f_{\\text{violet}} \\), whereas for a glass convex lens \\( f_{\\text{red}} > f_{\\text{violet}} \\).", "tex": "f_{\\text{ZP}} = \\frac{r_1^2}{(2m-1)\\lambda} \\; (f_R < f_V), \\quad \\frac{1}{f_{\\text{lens}}} = (n-1)\\left(\\frac{1}{R_1} - \\frac{1}{R_2}\\right) \\; (f_R > f_V)"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Focal length and chromatic dispersion comparison", "tex": "\\text{Zone plate: } f_m = \\frac{r_1^2}{(2m-1)\\lambda} \\implies \\lambda_R > \\lambda_V \\Rightarrow f_R < f_V \\\\ \\text{Convex lens: } \\frac{1}{f} = (n - 1)\\left(\\frac{1}{R_1} - \\frac{1}{R_2}\\right) \\implies n_V > n_R \\Rightarrow f_R > f_V", "body": "Compare the imaging formula, physical mechanism (diffraction vs refraction), number of foci, and chromatic aberration sign. Similarity & differences 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In a glass convex lens \\( f_{\\text{red}} > f_{\\text{violet}} \\), whereas in a Fresnel zone plate ____.", "options": ["f_red < f_violet", "f_red = f_violet", "f_red = infinity", "f_violet = 0"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Because f = r1^2 / lambda is inversely proportional to lambda, longer red wavelengths focus closer to the zone plate."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "All rays reaching the focus of a convex lens have equal optical paths, whereas waves from successive transparent zones of a zone plate differ in path by ____.", "options": ["one wavelength lambda", "zero", "lambda over 4", "half a wavelength"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Successive odd (or even) zones are two half-period zones apart, giving a path difference of 2*(lambda/2) = lambda."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Compared to a glass convex lens of equal aperture, the image formed at the principal focus of a zone plate is ____.", "options": ["much less intense", "100 percent efficient", "completely dark", "achromatic"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Half the area is opaque and light is also divided among zero and higher diffraction orders."}
          ]
