            {"type": "score", "title": "Q18 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. Fermat's principle states that the actual ray path between two points is the one for which the optical path length \\( L_{\\text{op}} = \\int n\\,ds \\) is an extremum (stationary). For reflection at plane mirror \\( MN \\) between \\( A(0, h_1) \\) and \\( B(L, h_2) \\), minimizing \\( L = \\sqrt{x^2 + h_1^2} + \\sqrt{(L-x)^2 + h_2^2} \\) gives \\( \\sin i = \\sin r \\implies i = r \\). For refraction across interface \\( PQ \\) between media \\( n_1 \\) and \\( n_2 \\), setting \\( \\frac{d}{dx}\\left[n_1\\sqrt{x^2 + h_1^2} + n_2\\sqrt{(L-x)^2 + h_2^2}\\right] = 0 \\) gives \\( n_1\\sin\\theta_1 = n_2\\sin\\theta_2 \\).", "tex": "i = r, \\quad n_1\\sin\\theta_1 = n_2\\sin\\theta_2"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Variational derivation of reflection and refraction laws", "tex": "\\text{1. Reflection: } L = AP + PB = \\sqrt{x^2 + h_1^2} + \\sqrt{(L - x)^2 + h_2^2} \\\\ \\frac{dL}{dx} = \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2 + h_1^2}} - \\frac{L - x}{\\sqrt{(L - x)^2 + h_2^2}} = \\sin i - \\sin r = 0 \\implies i = r \\\\ \\text{2. Refraction: } L_{\\text{op}} = n_1 AR + n_2 RB = n_1\\sqrt{x^2 + h_1^2} + n_2\\sqrt{(L - x)^2 + h_2^2} \\\\ \\frac{dL_{\\text{op}}}{dx} = \\frac{n_1 x}{\\sqrt{x^2 + h_1^2}} - \\frac{n_2(L - x)}{\\sqrt{(L - x)^2 + h_2^2}} = 0 \\implies n_1\\sin\\theta_1 = n_2\\sin\\theta_2", "body": "Write the optical path length for reflection and refraction as a function of incidence coordinate x and set dL_op / dx = 0. Principle & reflection 2 · refraction 2."},
            {
              "type": "derivation",
              "label": "Derivation",
              "title": "Snell's law of refraction from Fermat's principle",
              "legend": "Ray ARB connecting point A (height h1 in n1) to point B (depth h2 in n2) across interface PQ of horizontal span L.",
              "setup": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 260 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"90\" width=\"220\" height=\"75\" fill=\"#e8f0fe\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"55\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"55\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/><line x1=\"195\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"195\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/><line x1=\"125\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#555\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,2\"/><line x1=\"55\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"125\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"195\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><text x=\"48\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"10\">A</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"9\">h1</text><text x=\"85\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"9\">x</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"10\">R</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"9\">θ1</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"9\">θ2</text><text x=\"155\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"9\">L - x</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"9\">h2</text><text x=\"198\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"10\">B</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"10\">n1</text><text x=\"215\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"10\">n2</text></svg>",
              "phases": ["Optical path L_op(x)", "Differentiation dL_op/dx = 0", "Trigonometric identification", "Snell's law"],
              "steps": [
                {"phase": 0, "math": "L_{\\text{op}}(x) = n_1 AR + n_2 RB = n_1\\sqrt{x^2 + h_1^2} + n_2\\sqrt{(L - x)^2 + h_2^2}", "note": "Express the total optical path from A to B via point R(x) on interface PQ."},
                {"phase": 1, "math": "\\frac{dL_{\\text{op}}}{dx} = \\frac{n_1 x}{\\sqrt{x^2 + h_1^2}} - \\frac{n_2(L - x)}{\\sqrt{(L - x)^2 + h_2^2}} = 0", "note": "Differentiate L_op with respect to x and set the derivative to zero for a minimum."},
                {"phase": 2, "math": "\\sin\\theta_1 = \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2 + h_1^2}}, \\quad \\sin\\theta_2 = \\frac{L - x}{\\sqrt{(L - x)^2 + h_2^2}}", "note": "Identify sin(theta1) and sin(theta2) from the right triangles AMR and BNR."},
                {"phase": 3, "math": "n_1\\sin\\theta_1 - n_2\\sin\\theta_2 = 0 \\implies n_1\\sin\\theta_1 = n_2\\sin\\theta_2", "note": "Substitute the sines to obtain Snell's law of refraction."}
              ],
              "ask": [
                {"q": "Why must the incident ray, refracted ray, and normal all lie in the same plane?", "options": ["Any displacement of R out of the perpendicular plane through A and B increases both AR and RB", "Refractive indices are negative out of the plane", "Light is longitudinal", "The interface is curved"], "answer": 0, "why": "Projection onto the plane containing A, B and the normal is always shorter than any off-plane path."},
                {"q": "In the expression \\( L_{\\text{op}}(x) \\), which variable is varied to find the extremum ray path?", "options": ["The horizontal position x of point R on the interface", "The heights h1 and h2 of the fixed points A and B", "The refractive indices n1 and n2", "The speed of light c"], "answer": 0, "why": "A and B are fixed endpoints, while the intersection point R(x) on the boundary is varied."},
