          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 19", "marks": 4, "q": "What is system matrix ? Obtain it in the case of a system of two thin lenses separated by a distance and hence derive the formula for its focal length."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Definition of system matrix and product S = L2 T L1 for two thin lenses separated by d", "options": [{"t": "System matrix defined and product S = [[1, -1/f2], [0, 1]] [[1, 0], [d, 1]] [[1, -1/f1], [0, 1]] evaluated", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Matrices written without completing multiplication", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Define the system matrix and multiply L2 * T * L1 for two thin lenses of focal lengths f1, f2 separated by distance d in air."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Deduction of equivalent focal length formula 1/F = 1/f1 + 1/f2 - d/(f1 f2)", "options": [{"t": "Element -a = -1/F equated to -(1/f1 + 1/f2 - d/(f1 f2)) to obtain 1/F = 1/f1 + 1/f2 - d/(f1 f2)", "m": 1.5}, {"t": "Formula stated without connecting to matrix element", "m": 0.5}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Identify the optical power 1/F from the (1,2) element of the product matrix."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q19 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "System matrix and focal length of two separated thin lenses", "body": "Know first: The thin lens, principal foci and focal length. The system matrix is the \\( 2\\times 2 \\) matrix relating the output ray coordinates \\( (\\lambda_2, y_2) \\) to the input ray coordinates \\( (\\lambda_1, y_1) \\). For two thin lenses of focal lengths \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\) separated by distance \\( d \\) in air, \\( S = L_2 \\mathcal{T} L_1 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 - d/f_2 & -(1/f_1 + 1/f_2 - d/(f_1 f_2)) \\\\ d & 1 - d/f_1 \\end{bmatrix} \\). Since \\( S_{12} = -a = -1/F \\), the equivalent focal length is given by \\( \\frac{1}{F} = \\frac{1}{f_1} + \\frac{1}{f_2} - \\frac{d}{f_1 f_2} \\).", "tex": "S = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 - \\frac{d}{f_2} & -\\left(\\frac{1}{f_1} + \\frac{1}{f_2} - \\frac{d}{f_1 f_2}\\right) \\\\ d & 1 - \\frac{d}{f_1} \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\frac{1}{F} = \\frac{1}{f_1} + \\frac{1}{f_2} - \\frac{d}{f_1 f_2}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Matrix multiplication for two separated thin lenses", "tex": "L_1 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1/f_1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\mathcal{T} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ d & 1 \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad L_2 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1/f_2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\\\ S = L_2 \\mathcal{T} L_1 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1/f_2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1/f_1 \\\\ d & 1 - d/f_1 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 - \\frac{d}{f_2} & -\\left(\\frac{1}{f_1} + \\frac{1}{f_2} - \\frac{d}{f_1 f_2}\\right) \\\\ d & 1 - \\frac{d}{f_1} \\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\text{Comparing with } S = \\begin{bmatrix} b & -a \\\\ -d' & c \\end{bmatrix} \\text{ where } a = \\frac{1}{F}: \\quad \\frac{1}{F} = \\frac{1}{f_1} + \\frac{1}{f_2} - \\frac{d}{f_1 f_2}", "body": "Multiply L2 * T * L1 to obtain the 2x2 system matrix and read off the equivalent power 1/F from the (1,2) element. Definition & matrix product 2.5 · focal length formula 1.5."},
            {
              "type": "derivation",
              "label": "Derivation",
              "title": "System matrix and focal length of two separated thin lenses",
              "legend": "Two coaxial thin lenses of focal lengths f1 and f2 separated by distance d in air.",
              "setup": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 260 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><line x1=\"15\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"245\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"75\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#188038\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"165\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"68\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"10\">L1 (f1)</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"10\">L2 (f2)</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"10\">d</text><text x=\"225\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"10\">F</text></svg>",
              "phases": ["Individual lens matrices", "Intermediate product T L1", "Full product L2 T L1", "Equivalent focal length F"],
              "steps": [
                {"phase": 0, "math": "L_1 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1/f_1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\mathcal{T} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ d & 1 \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad L_2 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1/f_2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}", "note": "Write the thin-lens matrices for L1, L2 and the air translation matrix T for separation d."},
                {"phase": 1, "math": "\\mathcal{T} L_1 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ d & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1/f_1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1/f_1 \\\\ d & 1 - d/f_1 \\end{bmatrix}", "note": "Multiply the first lens matrix L1 by the translation matrix T."},
                {"phase": 2, "math": "S = L_2 \\mathcal{T} L_1 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 - \\frac{d}{f_2} & -\\left(\\frac{1}{f_1} + \\frac{1}{f_2} - \\frac{d}{f_1 f_2}\\right) \\\\ d & 1 - \\frac{d}{f_1} \\end{bmatrix}", "note": "Left-multiply by L2 to obtain the complete system matrix S."},
                {"phase": 3, "math": "a = -S_{12} = \\frac{1}{F} = \\frac{1}{f_1} + \\frac{1}{f_2} - \\frac{d}{f_1 f_2}", "note": "Equate the negative of the (1,2) entry to the equivalent power 1/F."}
              ],
              "ask": [
                {"q": "What is the translation matrix \\( \\mathcal{T} \\) for a distance \\( d \\) in air (\\( n = 1 \\))?", "options": ["[[1, 0], [d, 1]]", "[[1, -d], [0, 1]]", "[[d, 0], [0, d]]", "[[1, 0], [0, 1]]"], "answer": 0, "why": "In air (n = 1), y2 = y1 + d * lambda1 and lambda2 = lambda1."},
                {"q": "In what order are \\( L_1, \\mathcal{T}, L_2 \\) multiplied to form the system matrix \\( S \\)?", "options": ["L2 T L1", "L1 T L2", "T L1 L2", "L1 L2 T"], "answer": 0, "why": "The ray encounters L1 first, then T, then L2, so operators act from right to left as L2 T L1."},
                {"q": "Which entry of the system matrix \\( S \\) gives the negative of the equivalent power \\( -1/F \\)?", "options": ["The (1,2) entry S12", "The (2,1) entry S21", "The (1,1) entry S11", "The (2,2) entry S22"], "answer": 0, "why": "For a parallel input ray (lambda1 = 0), lambda2 = S12 y1 = -(1/F) y1."},
                {"q": "What happens to the equivalent power \\( 1/F \\) when the separation equals the sum of the focal lengths (\\( d = f_1 + f_2 \\), as in a telescope)?", "options": ["1/F = 0 (infinite focal length, afocal system)", "1/F = 2/f1", "F = 0", "1/F becomes negative infinity"], "answer": 0, "why": "When d = f1 + f2, 1/f1 + 1/f2 - (f1+f2)/(f1 f2) = 0."}
              ]
            },
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If two thin lenses of focal lengths \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\) are separated by a medium of refractive index \\( n \\) and thickness \\( d \\), the equivalent focal length satisfies \\( 1/F \\) equal to ____.", "options": ["1/f1 + 1/f2 - d/(n f1 f2)", "1/f1 + 1/f2 + n d/(f1 f2)", "(f1 + f2) / n", "d / (n f1 f2)"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Replacing d by the reduced distance d/n gives 1/F = 1/f1 + 1/f2 - d/(n f1 f2)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In Ramsden's and Huygens' eyepieces, two converging lenses are separated by a suitable distance \\( d \\) to minimize ____.", "options": ["chromatic and spherical aberrations", "light transmission", "resolving power", "numerical aperture"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Setting d = (f1 + f2)/2 makes the two-lens combination achromatic for all wavelengths."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The condition for achromatism of two thin lenses made of the same glass and separated by distance \\( d \\) in air is \\( d \\) equal to ____.", "options": ["(f1 + f2) / 2", "f1 - f2", "2(f1 + f2)", "sqrt(f1 f2)"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Differentiating 1/F with respect to n gives d = (f1 + f2)/2 for identical glass."}
          ]
        },
