          "cards": [
            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 24", "marks": 4, "q": "What is meant by critical angle of an optical fiber ? Obtain an expression for the critical angle."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Definition of critical angle at the core-cladding interface", "options": [{"t": "Minimum angle of incidence in the denser core (n1) for which the angle of refraction in the rarer cladding (n2) is 90 degrees, above which total internal reflection occurs", "m": 2}, {"t": "Partial definition", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Define the critical angle at the core-cladding boundary and its role in total internal reflection."},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Ray diagram and derivation of theta_c = sin^-1(n2 / n1)", "options": [{"t": "Diagram and Snell's law derivation n1 sin theta_c = n2 sin 90 = n2 => theta_c = sin^-1(n2/n1)", "m": 2}, {"t": "Formula stated without derivation", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Apply Snell's law at the core-cladding interface with angle of refraction r = 90 degrees."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q24 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Critical angle of an optical fiber", "body": "Know first: Laws of reflection and refraction from Fermat's principle. The critical angle \\( \\theta_c \\) of an optical fiber is the angle of incidence inside the denser core (refractive index \\( n_1 \\)) at the core-cladding boundary for which the refracted ray in the rarer cladding (refractive index \\( n_2 < n_1 \\)) grazes the interface at \\( r = 90^\\circ \\). Applying Snell's law \\( n_1\\sin\\theta_c = n_2\\sin 90^\\circ \\) gives \\( \\sin\\theta_c = \\frac{n_2}{n_1} \\), or \\( \\theta_c = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{n_2}{n_1}\\right) \\). Rays with \\( \\theta_i > \\theta_c \\) undergo total internal reflection.", "tex": "\\sin\\theta_c = \\frac{n_2}{n_1}, \\quad \\theta_c = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{n_2}{n_1}\\right)"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Derivation of critical angle expression", "tex": "\\text{Snell's law at core-cladding interface: } n_1\\sin\\theta_i = n_2\\sin\\theta_r \\\\ \\text{At critical angle } (\\theta_i = \\theta_c,\\; \\theta_r = 90^\\circ): \\quad n_1\\sin\\theta_c = n_2\\sin 90^\\circ = n_2 \\\\ \\sin\\theta_c = \\frac{n_2}{n_1} \\implies \\theta_c = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{n_2}{n_1}\\right) \\\\ \\cos\\theta_c = \\frac{\\sqrt{n_1^2 - n_2^2}}{n_1} = \\frac{\\text{NA}}{n_1}", "body": "Define the critical angle, draw the core-cladding grazing refraction ray, and set theta_r = 90 degrees in Snell's law. Definition 2 · diagram & derivation 2."},
            {
              "type": "derivation",
              "label": "Derivation",
              "title": "Critical angle at the core-cladding interface",
              "legend": "Ray in core (n1) incident at critical angle theta_c on cladding (n2 < n1) with refracted ray grazing along boundary (90 deg).",
              "setup": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 260 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"25\" width=\"220\" height=\"55\" fill=\"#e8f0fe\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"155\" stroke=\"#555\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,3\"/><line x1=\"55\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"235\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#188038\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#d93025\" stroke-dasharray=\"3,2\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"10\">Cladding (n2)</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"10\">Core (n1 > n2)</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"10\">θc</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"10\">90°</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"9\">TIR (θi > θc)</text></svg>",
              "phases": ["Snell's law at boundary", "Grazing refraction r = 90 deg", "Critical angle expression", "Relation to NA"],
              "steps": [
                {"phase": 0, "math": "n_1\\sin\\theta_i = n_2\\sin\\theta_r", "note": "Write Snell's law for a ray incident from the core (n1) onto the cladding (n2)."},
                {"phase": 1, "math": "\\theta_i = \\theta_c, \\quad \\theta_r = 90^\\circ \\implies \\sin\\theta_r = 1", "note": "Set the angle of refraction in the cladding equal to 90 degrees at the threshold of TIR."},
                {"phase": 2, "math": "n_1\\sin\\theta_c = n_2 \\implies \\theta_c = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{n_2}{n_1}\\right)", "note": "Solve for the critical angle theta_c."},
                {"phase": 3, "math": "\\cos\\theta_c = \\sqrt{1 - \\frac{n_2^2}{n_1^2}} = \\frac{\\text{NA}}{n_1}", "note": "Relate cos(theta_c) to the fiber's numerical aperture NA."}
              ],
              "ask": [
                {"q": "Why must \\( n_1 \\) be greater than \\( n_2 \\) for a real critical angle \\( \\theta_c \\) to exist?", "options": ["Because sin(theta_c) = n2/n1 cannot exceed 1", "Because n2 must be negative", "Because light speeds up in the core", "Because sin(90) = 0"], "answer": 0, "why": "For a real angle theta_c < 90 degrees, sin(theta_c) = n2/n1 must be less than 1."},
                {"q": "What is the angle of refraction \\( \\theta_r \\) in the cladding when \\( \\theta_i = \\theta_c \\)?", "options": ["90 degrees", "0 degrees", "45 degrees", "theta_c"], "answer": 0, "why": "At the critical angle, the refracted ray skims along the core-cladding interface."},
                {"q": "What happens to a ray inside the core when \\( \\theta_i > \\theta_c \\)?", "options": ["It undergoes total internal reflection back into the core", "It refracts straight into the cladding", "It stops moving", "It splits into o- and e-rays"], "answer": 0, "why": "Incidence angles exceeding theta_c are totally internally reflected."},
                {"q": "In a typical communication fiber where \\( n_1 \\approx 1.48 \\) and \\( n_2 \\approx 1.46 \\), the critical angle \\( \\theta_c \\) is close to ____.", "options": ["80.6 degrees (nearly grazing)", "10 degrees", "45 degrees", "0 degrees"], "answer": 0, "why": "When n2/n1 is close to 1, sin^-1(n2/n1) is close to 90 degrees (~80.6 degrees)."}
              ]
            },
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "If a fiber has \\( n_1 = 1.50 \\) and \\( n_2 = 1.47 \\), the sine of its critical angle \\( \\sin\\theta_c \\) is ____.", "options": ["1.47 / 1.50 = 0.98", "1.50 / 1.47", "0.03", "zero"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "sin(theta_c) = n2 / n1 = 1.47 / 1.50 = 0.98."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "In terms of the critical angle \\( \\theta_c \\), the maximum angle \\( \\theta_{\\text{axis}} \\) that a guided meridional ray can make with the fiber axis inside the core is ____.", "options": ["90 degrees minus theta_c", "theta_c", "2 theta_c", "90 degrees plus theta_c"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "The normal to the wall is perpendicular to the fiber axis, so theta_axis = 90 - theta_c."},
