            {"type": "question", "label": "PYQ · 4 marks", "title": "Question 25", "marks": 4, "q": "A soap film 5 \\times 10^{-5} cm thick is viewed at an angle of 35^\\circ to the normal. Find the wavelength of light in the visible spectrum which will be absent from the reflected light. Given \\mu = 1.33 ?"},
            {"type": "eval", "q": "Calculation of cos r from Snell's law and destructive wavelengths lambda = 2 mu d cos r / m", "options": [{"t": "cos r = 0.9003, 2 mu d cos r = 1.197 x 10^-4 cm, and visible absent wavelength for m = 2 is 5987 A (or for m = 3 is 3991 A)", "m": 4}, {"t": "Used i = 35 deg as r instead of applying Snell's law", "m": 2.5}, {"t": "Destructive condition 2 mu d cos r = m lambda stated only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Find sin r = sin(35 deg) / 1.33, compute 2 mu d cos r, and divide by integer m to find the wavelength in the visible range (4000 A - 7000 A)."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q25 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "Absent visible wavelength lambda = 5987 A (for m = 2)", "body": "Know first: Colours of thin films, Newton's rings, Michelson interferometer (11). By Snell's law, \\( \\sin r = \\frac{\\sin 35^\\circ}{1.33} = \\frac{0.5736}{1.33} = 0.4313 \\), so \\( \\cos r = \\sqrt{1 - 0.4313^2} = 0.9022 \\). For a wavelength to be absent (destructive interference) in reflected light, \\( 2\\mu d\\cos r = m\\lambda \\). With \\( d = 5\\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm} \\) and \\( \\mu = 1.33 \\), \\( 2\\mu d\\cos r = 1.200\\times 10^{-4}\\text{ cm} = 12000\\text{ \\AA} \\). For \\( m = 1, 2, 3 \\), \\( \\lambda = 12000\\text{ \\AA}, 6000\\text{ \\AA}, 4000\\text{ \\AA} \\); thus \\( \\lambda_2 = 6000\\text{ \\AA} \\) (and \\( \\lambda_3 = 4000\\text{ \\AA} \\) at the violet edge) is absent in the visible spectrum.", "tex": "\\lambda = 6.0 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm} = 6000\\text{ \\AA} \\; (m = 2)"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of destructive interference wavelength", "tex": "d = 5 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ cm}, \\quad i = 35^\\circ, \\quad \\mu = 1.33 \\\\ \\sin r = \\frac{\\sin 35^\\circ}{1.33} = \\frac{0.5736}{1.33} = 0.4313 \\implies \\cos r = \\sqrt{1 - 0.4313^2} = 0.9022 \\\\ \\text{Destructive condition in reflected light: } 2\\mu d\\cos r = m\\lambda \\\\ 2\\mu d\\cos r = 2 \\times 1.33 \\times 5 \\times 10^{-5} \\times 0.9022 = 1.200 \\times 10^{-4}\\text{ cm} = 12000\\text{ \\AA} \\\\ m = 1: \\lambda_1 = 12000\\text{ \\AA (IR)}; \\quad m = 2: \\lambda_2 = 6000\\text{ \\AA (Visible)}; \\quad m = 3: \\lambda_3 = 4000\\text{ \\AA (Violet edge)}", "body": "Find cos r using Snell's law, evaluate 2 mu d cos r = 12000 A, and test integer values m = 1, 2, 3 to select the wavelength inside the visible spectrum (4000–7000 A). cos r calculation 1.5 · 2 mu d cos r = m lambda 1.5 · visible selection 1."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "For a wavelength \\( \\lambda \\) to be absent (dark) in light reflected from a soap film in air, the condition is ____.", "options": ["2 mu d cos r = m lambda", "2 mu d cos r = (2m - 1) lambda / 2", "mu d sin r = m lambda", "d = m lambda"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Because of the pi phase shift at the top surface, 2 mu d cos(r) = m lambda gives destructive interference."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "The visible spectrum of light extends approximately from ____.", "options": ["4000 A to 7000 A (400 nm to 700 nm)", "100 A to 500 A", "10,000 A to 50,000 A", "1 mm to 10 cm"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "Human vision spans roughly 4000 A (violet) to 7000 A (red)."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "When light enters a soap film of refractive index \\( \\mu = 1.33 \\) from air at \\( i = 35^\\circ \\), the angle of refraction \\( r \\) is determined from ____.", "options": ["sin r = (sin 35 deg) / 1.33", "r = 35 degrees", "cos r = 1.33 cos 35 deg", "tan r = 1.33"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "By Snell's law, 1 * sin(i) = mu * sin(r)."}
