            {"type": "eval", "q": "Quarter-wave plate and half-wave plate thicknesses", "options": [{"t": "t_QWP = 2.16 x 10^-7 m (0.216 um) and t_HWP = 4.32 x 10^-7 m (0.432 um) calculated", "m": 4}, {"t": "Only one thickness calculated correctly", "m": 2}, {"t": "Formulas only", "m": 1}, {"t": "Missing or wrong", "m": 0}], "why": "Use mu_e - mu_o = 2.656 - 1.973 = 0.683 and lambda = 590 x 10^-9 m."},
            {"type": "score", "title": "Q27 · Your marks"},
            {"type": "info", "label": "Answer", "title": "(i) QWP = 0.216 um; (ii) HWP = 0.432 um", "body": "Know first: Quarter-wave and half-wave plates (21). With \\( \\lambda = 590\\text{ nm} = 5.90\\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} \\) and \\( \\mu_e - \\mu_o = 2.656 - 1.973 = 0.683 \\): (i) the thickness of the quarter-wave plate is \\( t_{\\text{QWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda}{4(\\mu_e - \\mu_o)} = \\frac{5.90\\times 10^{-7}}{4 \\times 0.683} = 2.160\\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} = 0.216\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} \\); (ii) the thickness of the half-wave plate is \\( t_{\\text{HWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda}{2(\\mu_e - \\mu_o)} = 4.319\\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} = 0.432\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} \\).", "tex": "t_{\\text{QWP}} = 2.16 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m}, \\quad t_{\\text{HWP}} = 4.32 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m}"},
            {"type": "math", "label": "Solution", "title": "Calculation of QWP and HWP thicknesses", "tex": "\\lambda = 590 \\times 10^{-9}\\text{ m}, \\quad \\Delta\\mu = \\mu_e - \\mu_o = 2.656 - 1.973 = 0.683 \\\\ \\text{(i) } t_{\\text{QWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda}{4(\\mu_e - \\mu_o)} = \\frac{5.90 \\times 10^{-7}}{4 \\times 0.683} = 2.160 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} = 0.216\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m} \\\\ \\text{(ii) } t_{\\text{HWP}} = \\frac{\\lambda}{2(\\mu_e - \\mu_o)} = \\frac{5.90 \\times 10^{-7}}{2 \\times 0.683} = 4.319 \\times 10^{-7}\\text{ m} = 0.432\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m}", "body": "Compute the birefringence mu_e - mu_o = 0.683 and evaluate the QWP and HWP thickness formulas. (i) QWP 2 · (ii) HWP 2."},
            {"type": "mcq", "q": "Because a single-order quarter-wave plate is often extremely thin and fragile, practical wave plates are frequently made with thickness equal to an ____.", "options": ["odd multiple (2m + 1) of the minimum QWP thickness", "even multiple 2m of the QWP thickness", "infinite thickness", "zero thickness"], "answer": 0, "time": 45, "practice": "remember-word", "why": "As shown in Eq. (22.53) of Ghatak, d = (2m + 1) lambda / [4|n_o - n_e|] gives a multi-order QWP."},
